<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<usx version="2.6">
  <book code="2KI" style="id">- Tov Rose New Messianic Version Bible</book>
  <para style="h">2 Kings</para>
  <para style="mt">2 Kings</para>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Then Mo’av <char style="add">[Seed of my Father]</char> rebelled against Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> after the death of Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And Achazyah <char style="add">[Yehovah possesses]</char> fell down through a lattice in his upper chamber that <char style="add">[was]</char> in Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>, and was injured: and he sent messengers, and said unto them, Go, enquire of Ba’al-Z’vuv <char style="add">[lord of the flies]</char> the god of ‘Ekron <char style="add">[Torn Up by the Roots]</char> whether I shall recover of this disease.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />But the angel of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said to Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char> the Tishbi <char style="add">[captivity]</char>, Arise, go up to meet the messengers of the king of Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>, and say unto them, <char style="add">[Is it]</char> not because <char style="add">[there is]</char> not a God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, <char style="add">[that]</char> you<char style="ord">2f</char> go to enquire of Ba’al-Z’vuv <char style="add">[lord of the flies]</char> the god of ‘Ekron <char style="add">[Torn Up by the Roots]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Now therefore thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, you<char style="ord">i</char> shall not come down from that bed on which you<char style="ord">i</char> are gone up, but shall surely die. And Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char> departed.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And when the messengers turned back unto him, he said unto them, Why are you<char style="ord">2f</char> now turned back?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And they said unto him, There came a man up to meet us, and said unto us, Go, turn again unto the king that sent you, and say unto him, Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, <char style="add">[Is it]</char> not because <char style="add">[there is]</char> not a God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, <char style="add">[that]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> send to enquire of Ba’al-Z’vuv <char style="add">[lord of the flies]</char> the god of ‘Ekron <char style="add">[Torn Up by the Roots]</char>? therefore you<char style="ord">i</char> shall not come down from that bed on which you<char style="ord">i</char> are gone up, but shall surely die.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And he said unto them, What manner of man <char style="add">[was he]</char> which came up to meet you, and told you these words?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And they answered him, <char style="add">[He was]</char> an hairy man, and wearing with a belt of leather about his waist. And he said, It <char style="add">[is]</char> Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char> the Tishbi <char style="add">[captivity]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Then the king sent unto him a captain of fifty with his fifty. And he went up to him: and, behold, he sat on the top of an hill. And he spoke unto him, you<char style="ord">i</char> man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, the king has said, Come down.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char> answered and said to the captain of fifty, If I <char style="add">[be]</char> a man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, then let fire come down from heaven, and consume you<char style="ord">i</char> and your<char style="ord">i</char> fifty. And there came down fire from heaven, and consumed him and his fifty.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Again also he sent unto him another captain of fifty with his fifty. And he answered and said unto him, O man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, thus has the king said, Come down quickly.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char> answered and said unto them, If I <char style="add">[be]</char> a man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, let fire come down from heaven, and consume you<char style="ord">i</char> and your<char style="ord">i</char> fifty. And the fire of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> came down from heaven, and consumed him and his fifty.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And he sent again a captain of the third fifty with his fifty. And the third captain of fifty went up, and came and fell on his knees before Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char>, and besought him, and said unto him, O man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, let my life, and the life of these fifty your<char style="ord">i</char> servants, be precious in your<char style="ord">i</char> sight.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Behold, there came fire down from heaven, and burnt up the two captains of the former fifties with their fifties: therefore let my life now be precious in your<char style="ord">i</char> sight.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And the angel <char style="pn">(messenger)</char> of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char>, Go down with him: be not afraid of him. And he arose, and went down with him unto the king.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And he said unto him, Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, Forasmuch as you<char style="ord">i</char> have sent messengers to enquire of Ba’al-Z’vuv <char style="add">[lord of the flies]</char> the god of ‘Ekron <char style="add">[Torn Up by the Roots]</char>, <char style="add">[is it]</char> not because <char style="add">[there is]</char> no God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> to enquire of his word? therefore you<char style="ord">i</char> shall not come down off that bed on which you<char style="ord">i</char> are gone up, but shall surely die.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />So he died according to the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> which Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char> had spoken. And Y’horam <char style="add">[Yehovah is exalted]</char> reigned in his stead in the second year of Y’horam <char style="add">[Yehovah is exalted]</char> the son of Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>; because he had no son.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Now the rest of the acts of Achazyah <char style="add">[Yehovah possesses]</char> which he did, <char style="add">[are]</char> they not written in the book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>?</para>
  <chapter number="2" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And it came to pass, when the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> would take up Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char> into heaven by a whirlwind, that Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char> went with Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char> from Gilgal <char style="add">[A Wheel, Rolling]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char> said unto Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char>, Tarry here, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>; for the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has sent me to Beit-El <char style="add">[House of God]</char>. And Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char> said <char style="add">[unto him, As]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> lives, and <char style="add">[as]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> soul lives, I will not leave you<char style="ord">i</char>. So they went down to Beit-El <char style="add">[House of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And the sons of the prophets that <char style="add">[were]</char> at Beit-El <char style="add">[House of God]</char> came forth to Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char>, and said unto him, Know you<char style="ord">i</char> that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> will take away your<char style="ord">i</char> master from your<char style="ord">i</char> head to day? And he said, Yes, I know <char style="add">[it]</char>; hold you<char style="ord">2f</char> your peace <char style="pn">(say no more)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char> said unto him, Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char>, wait here, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>; for the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has sent me to Yericho <char style="add">[Its Moon]</char>. And he said, <char style="add">[As]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> lives, and <char style="add">[as]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> soul lives, I will not leave you<char style="ord">i</char>. So they came to Yericho <char style="add">[Its Moon]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And the sons of the prophets that <char style="add">[were]</char> at Yericho <char style="add">[Its Moon]</char> came to Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char>, and said unto him, Know you<char style="ord">i</char> that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> will take away your<char style="ord">i</char> master from your<char style="ord">i</char> head to day? And he answered, Yes, I know <char style="add">[it]</char>; hold you<char style="ord">2f</char> your peace.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char> said unto him, Tarry here I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>; for the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has sent me to Yarden <char style="add">[Descender]</char>. And he said, <char style="add">[As]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> lives, and <char style="add">[as]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> soul lives, I will not leave you<char style="ord">i</char>. And they two went on.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And fifty men of the sons of the prophets went, and stood to view afar off: and they two stood by Yarden <char style="add">[Descender]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char> took his Mantle <char style="pn">(cloak; covering garment)</char> <char style="pn">(cloak)</char>, and wrapped <char style="add">[it]</char> together, and struck the waters, and they were divided to the right and left, so that they two went over on dry ground.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And it came to pass, when they were gone over, that Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char> said unto Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char>, Ask what I shall do for you<char style="ord">i</char>, before I be taken away from you<char style="ord">i</char>. And Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char> said, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, let a double portion of your<char style="ord">i</char> spirit be upon me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And he said, you<char style="ord">i</char> have asked a hard thing: <char style="add">[nevertheless]</char>, if you<char style="ord">i</char> see me <char style="add">[when I am]</char> taken from you<char style="ord">i</char>, it shall be so unto you<char style="ord">i</char>; but if not, it shall not be <char style="add">[so]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And it came to pass, as they still went on, and talked, that, behold, <char style="add">[there appeared]</char> a chariot of fire, and horses of fire, and it separated them both; and Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char> went up by a whirlwind into heaven.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char> saw <char style="add">[it]</char>, and he cried, My father! my father! the chariot and the horsemen of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>! And he lost sight of him: and he took hold of his own clothes, and tore them in two pieces.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />He took up also the Mantle <char style="pn">(cloak; covering garment)</char> <char style="pn">(cloak)</char> of Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char> that fell from him, and went back, and stood by the bank of Yarden <char style="add">[Descender]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And he took the Mantle <char style="pn">(cloak; covering garment)</char> <char style="pn">(cloak)</char> of Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char> that fell from him, and struck the waters, and said, Where <char style="add">[is]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char>? and when he also had smitten the waters, they parted to the right and to the left: and Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char> went over.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And when the sons of the prophets which <char style="add">[were]</char> to view at Yericho <char style="add">[Its Moon]</char> saw him, they said, The spirit of Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char> does rest on Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char>. And they came to meet him, and bowed themselves to the ground before him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And they said unto him, Behold now, there be with your<char style="ord">i</char> servants fifty strong men; let them go, we pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, and seek your<char style="ord">i</char> master: in the event perhaps the Spirit of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has taken him up, and cast him upon some mountain, or into some valley. And he said, You<char style="ord">2f</char> shall not send.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And when they urged him till he was ashamed, he said, Send. They sent therefore fifty men; and they sought three days, but found him not.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And when they came again to him, (for he tarried at Yericho <char style="add">[Its Moon]</char>,) he said unto them, Did I not say unto you, Go not?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And the men of the city said unto Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char>, Behold, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, the situation of this city <char style="add">[is]</char> pleasant, as my lord sees: but the water <char style="add">[is]</char> bad, and the ground barren.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And he said, Bring me a new jug, and put salt in it. And they brought <char style="add">[it]</char> to him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And he went forth unto the spring of the waters, and cast the salt in there, and said, Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, I have healed these waters; there shall not be from there any more death or barren <char style="add">[land]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />So the waters were healed unto this day, according to the saying of Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char> which he spoke.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And he went up from there unto Beit-El <char style="add">[House of God]</char>: and as he was going up by the way, there came forth young men out of the city, and mocked him, and said unto him, Go up, you<char style="ord">i</char> bald head; go up, you<char style="ord">i</char> bald head.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And he turned back, and looked on them, and cursed them in the name of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>. And there came forth two she bears out of the wood, and tare forty and two children of them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And he went from there to mount Carmel <char style="add">[Garden-land]</char>, and from there he returned to Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="3" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Now Y’horam <char style="add">[Yehovah is exalted]</char> the son of Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> began to reign over Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> in Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char> the eighteenth year of Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and reigned twelve years.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And he wrought evil in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; but not like his father, and like his mother: for he put away the image of Ba’al <char style="add">[lord (a false god)]</char> that his father had made.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Nevertheless he cleaved unto the sins of Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> the son of N’vat <char style="add">[aspect]</char>, which made Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> to sin; he departed not from them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And Mesha <char style="add">[deliverance]</char> king of Mo’av <char style="add">[Seed of my Father]</char> was a sheep-breeder, and rendered unto the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> an hundred thousand lambs, and an hundred thousand rams, with the wool.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />But it came to pass, when Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> was dead, that the king of Mo’av <char style="add">[Seed of my Father]</char> rebelled against the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And king Y’horam <char style="add">[Yehovah is exalted]</char> went out of Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char> the same time, and numbered all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And he went and sent to Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> the king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, saying, The king of Mo’av <char style="add">[Seed of my Father]</char> has rebelled against me: will you<char style="ord">i</char> go with me against Mo’av <char style="add">[Seed of my Father]</char> to battle? And he said, I will go up: I <char style="add">[am]</char> as you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[are]</char>, my people as your<char style="ord">i</char> people, <char style="add">[and]</char> my horses as your<char style="ord">i</char> horses.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And he said, Which way shall we go up? And he answered, The way through the wilderness of Edom <char style="add">[Red]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />So the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> went, and the king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and the king of Edom <char style="add">[Red]</char>: and they went on a circular course <char style="pn">(go around, encircle; encompass)</char> of seven days’ journey: and there was no water for the host, and for the cattle that followed them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> said, Alas! that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has called these three kings together, to deliver them into the hand of Mo’av <char style="add">[Seed of my Father]</char>!</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />But Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> said, <char style="add">[Is there]</char> not here a prophet of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, that we may enquire of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> by him? And one of the king of Yisra’el’s <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> servants answered and said, Here <char style="add">[is]</char> Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char> the son of Shafat <char style="add">[He Has Judged]</char>, which poured water on the hands of Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> said, The word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> is with him. So the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> and Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> and the king of Edom <char style="add">[Red]</char> went down to him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char> said unto the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, What have I to do with you<char style="ord">i</char>? get you<char style="ord">i</char> to the prophets of your<char style="ord">i</char> father, and to the prophets of your<char style="ord">i</char> mother. And the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> said unto him, No: for the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has called these three kings together, to deliver them into the hand of Mo’av <char style="add">[Seed of my Father]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char> said, <char style="add">[As]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char> lives, before whom I stand, surely, were it not that I regard the presence of Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> the king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, I would not look toward you<char style="ord">i</char>, nor see you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />But now bring me a musician. And it came to pass, when the musician played, that the hand of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came upon him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And he said, Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, Make this valley full of trenches.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />For thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, You<char style="ord">2f</char> shall not see wind, neither shall you<char style="ord">2f</char> see rain; yet that valley shall be filled with water, that you<char style="ord">2f</char> may drink, both you<char style="ord">2f</char>, and your cattle, and your beasts.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And this is <char style="add">[but]</char> a light thing in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: he will deliver the Mo’avi <char style="add">[of his father]</char> also into your hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall strike every fenced city, and every choice city, and shall fell every good tree, and stop all wells of water, and ruin every good piece of land with stones.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And it came to pass in the morning, when the meat offering was offered, that, behold, there came water by the way of Edom <char style="add">[Red]</char>, and the country was filled with water.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And when all the Mo’avi <char style="add">[of his father]</char> heard that the kings were come up to fight against them, they gathered all that were able to put on armour, and upward, and stood in the border.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And they rose up early in the morning, and the sun shone upon the water, and the Mo’avi <char style="add">[of his father]</char> saw the water on the other side <char style="add">[as]</char> red as blood:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And they said, This <char style="add">[is]</char> blood: the kings are surely slain, and they have smitten one another: now therefore, Mo’av <char style="add">[Seed of my Father]</char>, to the spoil <char style="pn">(plunder; prey; booty)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And when they came to the camp of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, the Yisra’eli’s rose up and struck the Mo’avi <char style="add">[of his father]</char>, so that they fled before them: but they went forward attacking the Mo’avi <char style="add">[of his father]</char>, even in <char style="add">[their]</char> country.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And they beat down the cities, and on every good piece of land cast every man his stone, and filled it; and they stopped all the wells of water, and felled all the good trees: only in Kir-Hareset <char style="add">[wall of potsherds]</char> left they the stones thereof; howbeit the slingers went about <char style="add">[it]</char>, and struck it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And when the king of Mo’av <char style="add">[Seed of my Father]</char> saw that the battle was too much for him, he took with him seven hundred men that drew swords, to break through <char style="add">[even]</char> unto the king of Edom <char style="add">[Red]</char>: but they could not.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />Then he took his eldest son that should have reigned in his stead, and offered him <char style="add">[for]</char> a burnt offering upon the wall. And there was great indignation against Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: and they departed from him, and returned to <char style="add">[their own]</char> land.</para>
  <chapter number="4" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Now there cried a certain woman of the wives of the sons of the prophets unto Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char>, saying, Your<char style="ord">1s</char> servant my husband is dead; and you<char style="ord">i</char> know that your<char style="ord">i</char> servant did fear the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: and the creditor is come to take with him my two sons to be slaves.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char> said unto her, What shall I do for you<char style="ord">i</char>? tell me, what have you<char style="ord">i</char> in the house? And she said, Your<char style="ord">1s</char> female servant has not anything in the house, save a pot of oil.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Then he said, Go, borrow you<char style="ord">i</char> containers from all your<char style="ord">i</char> neighbours, <char style="add">[even]</char> empty vessels; borrow not a few.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And when you<char style="ord">i</char> are come in, you<char style="ord">i</char> shall shut the door upon you<char style="ord">i</char> and upon your<char style="ord">i</char> sons, and shall pour out into all those vessels, and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall set aside that which is full.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />So she went from him, and shut the door upon her and upon her sons, who brought <char style="add">[the vessels]</char> to her; and she poured out.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And it came to pass, when the vessels were full, that she said unto her son, Bring me another vessel. And he said unto her, <char style="add">[There is]</char> not a vessel more. And the oil stopped flowing.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Then she came and told the man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>. And he said, Go, sell the oil, and pay your<char style="ord">i</char> debt, and live you<char style="ord">i</char> and your<char style="ord">i</char> children off the rest.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And it fell on a day, that Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char> passed to Shunem <char style="add">[Double Resting Place]</char>, where <char style="add">[was]</char> a well-to-do woman; and she constrained him to eat bread. And <char style="add">[so]</char> it was, <char style="add">[that]</char> as oft as he passed by, he turned in there to eat bread.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And she said unto her husband, Behold now, I perceive that this <char style="add">[is]</char> an holy man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, which passes by us continually.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Let us make a little chamber, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, on the wall; and let us set for him there a bed, and a table, and a stool, and a candlestick: and it shall be, when he comes to us, that he shall turn in there.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And it fell on a day, that he came there, and he turned into the chamber, and lay there.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And he said to Geichazi <char style="add">[valley of vision]</char> his servant, Call this Shunamit <char style="add">[double resting place]</char>. And when he had called her, she stood before him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And he said unto him, Say now unto her, Behold, you<char style="ord">i</char> have shown us so much hospitality; what <char style="add">[is]</char> to be done for you<char style="ord">i</char>? would you<char style="ord">i</char> be spoken for to the king, or to the captain of the host? And she answered, I dwell among my own people.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And he said, What then <char style="add">[is]</char> to be done for her? And Geichazi <char style="add">[valley of vision]</char> answered, Truly she has no child, and her husband is old.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And he said, Call her. And when he had called her, she stood in the door.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And he said, About this season, according to the time of life, you<char style="ord">i</char> shall embrace a son. And she said, No, my lord, <char style="pn">[you<char style="ord">i</char>]</char> man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, do not lie unto your<char style="ord">i</char> female servant.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And the woman conceived, and bore a son at that season that Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char> had said unto her, according to the time of life.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And when the child was grown, it fell on a day, that he went out to his father to the reapers.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And he said unto his father, My head, my head. And he said to a boy, Carry him to his mother.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And when he had taken him, and brought him to his mother, he sat on her knees till noon, and <char style="add">[then]</char> died.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And she went up, and laid him on the bed of the man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and shut <char style="add">[the door]</char> upon him, and went out.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And she called unto her husband, and said, Send me, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, one of the young men, and one of the asses, that I may run to the man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and come again.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And he said, For what reason will you<char style="ord">i</char> go to him to day? <char style="add">[it is]</char> neither new moon, nor Shabbat <char style="add">[Rest]</char>. And she said, <char style="add">[It shall be]</char> well <char style="pn">(It will be alright)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />Then she saddled an ass, and said to her servant, Drive, and go forward; slack not <char style="add">[your<char style="ord">i</char>]</char> riding for me, unless I say so to you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />So she went and came unto the man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> to mount Carmel <char style="add">[Garden-land]</char>. And it came to pass, when the man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> saw her afar off, that he said to Geichazi <char style="add">[valley of vision]</char> his servant, Behold, <char style="add">[over there is]</char> that Shunamit <char style="add">[double resting place]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />Run now, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, to meet her, and say unto her, <char style="add">[Is it]</char> well with you<char style="ord">i</char>? <char style="add">[is it]</char> well with you<char style="ord">i</char> husband? <char style="add">[is it]</char> well with the child? And she answered, <char style="add">[It is]</char> well.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And when she came to the man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> to the hill, she caught him by the feet: but Geichazi <char style="add">[valley of vision]</char> came near to thrust her away. And the man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> said, Let her alone; for her soul <char style="add">[is]</char> vexed within her: and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has hid <char style="add">[it]</char> from me, and has not told me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />Then she said, Did I desire a son of my lord? did I not say, Do not deceive me?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />Then he said to Geichazi <char style="add">[valley of vision]</char>, Get dressed for action, and take my staff in your<char style="ord">i</char> hand, and go on your<char style="ord">i</char> way: if you<char style="ord">i</char> meet any man, salute him not; and if any salute you<char style="ord">i</char>, answer him not again: and lay my staff upon the face of the child.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And the mother of the child said, <char style="add">[As]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> lives, and <char style="add">[as]</char> yorui soul lives, I will not leave you<char style="ord">i</char>. And he arose, and followed her.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And Geichazi <char style="add">[valley of vision]</char> passed on before them, and laid the staff upon the face of the child; but <char style="add">[there was]</char> neither voice, nor hearing. For this reason he went again to meet him <char style="pn">(Eli-sha)</char>, and told him, saying, The child is not awakened.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />And when Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char> was come into the house, behold, the child was dead, <char style="add">[and]</char> laid upon his bed.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />He went in therefore, and shut the door upon them both, and prayed unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />And he went up, and lay upon the child, and put his mouth upon his mouth, and his eyes upon his eyes, and his hands upon his hands: and he stretched himself upon the child; and the flesh of the child grew warm.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />Then he went down, and walked in the house to and fro; and went up, and stretched himself upon him: and the child sneezed seven times, and the child opened his eyes.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />And he called Geichazi <char style="add">[valley of vision]</char>, and said, Call this Shunamit <char style="add">[double resting place]</char>. So he called her. And when she was come in unto him, he said, Take up your<char style="ord">i</char> son.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" />Then she went in, and fell at his feet, and bowed herself to the ground, and took up her son, and went out.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" />And Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char> came again to Gilgal <char style="add">[A Wheel, Rolling]</char>: and <char style="add">[there was]</char> a famine in the land; and the sons of the prophets <char style="add">[were]</char> sitting before him: and he said unto his servant, Set on the great pot, and seethe pottage for the sons of the prophets.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" />And one went out into the field to gather herbs, and found a wild vine, and gathered thereof wild gourds his lap full, and came and shred <char style="add">[them]</char> into the pot of pottage: they didn’t know what they were.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="40" style="v" />So they poured out for the men to eat. And it came to pass, as they were eating of the pottage, that they cried out, and said, O <char style="pn">[you<char style="ord">i</char>]</char> man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, <char style="add">[there is]</char> death in the pot. And they could not eat <char style="add">[of it]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="41" style="v" />But he said, Then bring flour. And he cast <char style="add">[it]</char> into the pot; and he said, Pour out for the people, that they may eat. And there was nothing harmful in the pot.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="42" style="v" />And there came a man from Ba’al-Shalishah <char style="add">[thrice-great lord]</char>, and brought the man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> bread of the firstfruits, twenty loaves of barley, and full ears of corn in the husk thereof. And he said, Give unto the people, that they may eat.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="43" style="v" />And his servant said, How should I set this before an hundred men? He said again, Give the people, that they may eat: for thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, They shall eat, and shall have some leftover of it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="44" style="v" />So he set <char style="add">[it]</char> before them, and they did eat, and had some left over, according to the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="5" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Now Na’aman <char style="add">[Pleasantness]</char>, captain of the host of the king of Aram <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char>, was a great man with his master, and honourable, because by him the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had given deliverance unto Aram <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char>: he was also a mighty man in valour, <char style="add">[but he was]</char> a leper.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And the Aram <char style="add">[Syrians]</char> had gone out by companies, and had brought away captive out of the land of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> a little maid; and she waited on Na’aman <char style="add">[Pleasantness]</char>’s wife.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And she said unto her mistress, Would God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> my lord <char style="add">[were]</char> with the prophet that <char style="add">[is]</char> in Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>! for he would heal him of his leprosy.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And <char style="add">[one]</char> went in, and told his lord, saying, Thus and thus said the maid that <char style="add">[is]</char> of the land of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And the king of Aram <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char> said, Go ahead, go, and I will send a letter unto the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>. And he departed, and took with him ten talents of silver, and six thousand <char style="add">[pieces]</char> of gold, and ten changes of clothing.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And he brought the letter to the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, saying, Now when this letter is come unto you<char style="ord">i</char>, behold, I have <char style="add">[along with it]</char> sent Na’aman <char style="add">[Pleasantness]</char> my servant to you<char style="ord">i</char>, that you<char style="ord">i</char> may heal him of his leprosy.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And it came to pass, when the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> had read the letter, that he rent his clothes, and said, <char style="add">[Am]</char> I God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, to kill and to make alive, that this man does send unto me to heal a man of his leprosy? Therefore consider, I pray you, and see how he seeks a quarrel against me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And it was <char style="add">[so]</char>, when Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char> the man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> had heard that the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> had rent his clothes, that he sent to the king, saying, For what reason have you<char style="ord">i</char> rent your<char style="ord">i</char> clothes? let him come now to me, and he shall know that there is a prophet in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />So Na’aman <char style="add">[Pleasantness]</char> came with his horses and with his chariot, and stood at the door of the house of Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char> sent a messenger unto him, saying, Go and wash in Yarden <char style="add">[Descender]</char> seven times, and your<char style="ord">i</char> flesh shall come again to you<char style="ord">i</char>, and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall be clean.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />But Na’aman <char style="add">[Pleasantness]</char> was exceedingly angry, and went away, and said, Behold, I thought, He will surely come out to me, and stand, and call on the name of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> his God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and wave his hand over the place, and heal the leper.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[Are]</char> not Amanah <char style="pn">(Avnah)</char> <char style="add">[faith, support]</char> and Parpar <char style="add">[swift]</char>, rivers of Dammesek <char style="pn">(Damascus)</char> <char style="add">[silent is the sackcloth weaver]</char>, better than all the waters of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>? may I not wash in them, and be clean? So he turned and went away in a rage.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And his servants came near, and spoke unto him, and said, My father, <char style="add">[if]</char> the prophet had bid you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[do some]</char> difficult thing, would you<char style="ord">i</char> not have done <char style="add">[it]</char>? how much rather then, when he says to you<char style="ord">i</char>, Wash, and be clean?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Then went he down, and dipped himself seven times in Yarden <char style="add">[Descender]</char>, according to the saying of the man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>: and his flesh came again like unto the flesh of a little child, and he was clean.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And he returned to the man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, he and all his company, and came, and stood before him: and he said, Behold, now I know that <char style="add">[there is]</char> no God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> in all the earth, but in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: now therefore, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, take a blessing of your<char style="ord">i</char> servant.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />But he said, <char style="add">[As]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> lives, before whom I stand, I will receive none. And he urged him to take <char style="add">[it]</char>; but he refused.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And Na’aman <char style="add">[Pleasantness]</char> said, Shall there not then, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, be given to your<char style="ord">i</char> servant two mules’ burden of earth? for your<char style="ord">i</char> servant will from this time forward offer neither burnt offering nor sacrifice unto other gods, but unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />In this thing the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> pardon your<char style="ord">i</char> servant, <char style="add">[that]</char> when my master goes into the house of Rimmon <char style="add">[Pomegranate]</char> to worship there, and he leans on my hand, and I bow myself in the house of Rimmon <char style="add">[Pomegranate]</char>: when I bow down myself in the house of Rimmon <char style="add">[Pomegranate]</char>, the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> pardon your<char style="ord">i</char> servant in this thing.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And he said unto him, Go in peace. So he departed from him after a short distance.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />But Geichazi <char style="add">[valley of vision]</char>, the servant of Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char> the man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, said, Behold, my master has spared Na’aman <char style="add">[Pleasantness]</char> this Arami <char style="add">[exalted]</char>, in not receiving at his hands that which he brought: but, <char style="add">[as]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> lives, I will run after him, and take something of him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />So Geichazi <char style="add">[valley of vision]</char> followed after Na’aman <char style="add">[Pleasantness]</char>. And when Na’aman <char style="add">[Pleasantness]</char> saw <char style="add">[him]</char> running after him, he came down from the chariot to meet him, and said, <char style="add">[Is]</char> all well?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And he said, All <char style="add">[is]</char> well. My master has sent me, saying, Behold, even now there be come to me from mount Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char> two young men of the sons of the prophets: give them, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, a talent <char style="pn">(weight of money; weight; gift)</char> of silver, and two changes of garments.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And Na’aman <char style="add">[Pleasantness]</char> said, Be content, take two talents. And he urged him, and bound two talents of silver in two bags, with two changes of garments, and laid <char style="add">[them]</char> upon two of his servants; and they carried <char style="add">[them]</char> before him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And when he came to the tower, he took <char style="add">[them]</char> from their hand, and placed <char style="add">[them]</char> in the house: and he let the men go, and they departed.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />But he went in, and stood before his master. And Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char> said unto him, From where do you<char style="ord">i</char> come, Geichazi <char style="add">[valley of vision]</char>? And he said, Your<char style="ord">1s</char> servant went nowhere.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And he said unto him, Went not my heart [with you<char style="ord">i</char>], when the man turned again from his chariot to meet you<char style="ord">i</char>? <char style="add">[Is it]</char> a time to receive money, and to receive garments, and olive yards, and vineyards, and sheep, and oxen, and menservants, and maidservants?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />The leprosy therefore of Na’aman <char style="add">[Pleasantness]</char> shall cling unto you<char style="ord">i</char>, and unto your<char style="ord">i</char> descendants forever. And he went out from his presence a leper <char style="add">[as white]</char> as snow.</para>
  <chapter number="6" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And the sons of the prophets said unto Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char>, Behold now, the place where we dwell with you<char style="ord">i</char> is too small for us.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Let us go, we pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, unto Yarden <char style="add">[Descender]</char>, and take there every man a beam, and let us make us a place there, where we may dwell. And he answered, Go you<char style="ord">2f</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And one said, Be content, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, and go with your<char style="ord">i</char> servants. And he answered, I will go.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />So he went with them. And when they came to Yarden <char style="add">[Descender]</char>, they cut down wood.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />But as one was felling a beam, the axe head fell into the water: and he cried, and said, Alas, master! for it was borrowed.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And the man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> said, Where fell it? And he showed him the place. And he cut down a stick, and cast <char style="add">[it]</char> in there; and the iron did swim.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Therefore said he, Take <char style="add">[it]</char> up to you<char style="ord">i</char>. And he put out his hand, and took it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Then the king of Aram <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char> warred against Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and took counsel with his servants, saying, In such and such a place <char style="add">[shall be]</char> my camp.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And the man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> sent unto the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, saying, Beware that you<char style="ord">i</char> pass not such a place; for there the Aram <char style="add">[Syrians]</char> are come down.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> sent to the place which the man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> told him and warned him of, and saved himself there, more than once or twice.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Therefore the heart of the king of Aram <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char> was greatly troubled for this thing; and he called his servants, and said unto them, Will you<char style="ord">2f</char> not show me which of us <char style="add">[is]</char> <char style="pn">(a traitor)</char> for the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And one of his servants said, None, my lord, O king: but Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char>, the prophet that <char style="add">[is]</char> in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, tells the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> the words that you<char style="ord">i</char> speak in your<char style="ord">i</char> bedchamber.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And he said, Go and spy where he <char style="add">[is]</char>, that I may send and fetch him. And it was told him, saying, Behold, <char style="add">[he is]</char> in Dotan <char style="add">[two wells]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Therefore sent he there horses, and chariots, and a great host: and they came by night, and surrounded the city about.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And when the servant of the man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> was risen early, and gone forth, behold, an host compassed the city both with horses and chariots. And his servant said unto him, This is terrible, my master! what shall we do?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And he answered, Fear not: for they that <char style="add">[be]</char> with us <char style="add">[are]</char> more than they that <char style="add">[be]</char> with them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char> prayed, and said, LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, open his eyes, that he may see. And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> opened the eyes of the young man; and he saw: and, behold, the mountain <char style="add">[was]</char> full of horses and chariots of fire round about Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And when they came down to him, Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char> prayed unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and said, Strike this people, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, with blindness. And He struck them with blindness according to the word of Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char> said unto them, This <char style="add">[is]</char> not the way, neither <char style="add">[is]</char> this the city: follow me, and I will bring you to the man whom you<char style="ord">2f</char> seek. But he led them to Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And it came to pass, when they were come into Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>, that Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char> said, LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, open the eyes of these <char style="add">[men]</char>, that they may see. And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> opened their eyes, and they saw; and, behold, <char style="add">[they were]</char> in the midst of Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> said unto Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char>, when he saw them, My father, shall I strike <char style="add">[them]</char>? shall I strike <char style="add">[them]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And he answered, you<char style="ord">i</char> shall not strike <char style="add">[them]</char>: would you<char style="ord">i</char> strike those whom you<char style="ord">i</char> have taken captive with your<char style="ord">i</char> sword and with your<char style="ord">i</char> bow? set bread and water before them, that they may eat and drink, and go to their master.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And he prepared great provision for them: and when they had eaten and drunk, he sent them away, and they went to their master. So the bands of Aram <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char> came no more into the land of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And it came to pass after this, that Ben-Hadad [son of the <char style="pn">(false god)</char> Hadad] king of Aram <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char> gathered all his host, and went up, and besieged Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And there was a great famine in Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>: and, behold, they besieged it, until an ass’s head was <char style="add">[sold]</char> for eighty <char style="add">[pieces]</char> of silver, and the fourth part of a half a pint of dove’s dung for five <char style="add">[pieces]</char> of silver.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And as the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> was passing by upon the wall, there cried a woman unto him, saying, Help, my lord, O king.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And he said, If the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> do not help you<char style="ord">i</char>, in from where shall I <char style="add">[find]</char> help you<char style="ord">i</char>? out of the barn floor, or out of the winepress?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And the king said unto her, What ails you<char style="ord">i</char>? And she answered, This woman said unto me, Give your<char style="ord">i</char> son, that we may eat him to day, and we will eat my son tomorrow.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />So we boiled my son, and did eat him: and I said unto her on the next day, Give your<char style="ord">i</char> son, that we may eat him: and she has hid her son.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And it came to pass, when the king heard the words of the woman, that he rent his clothes; and he passed by upon the wall, and the people looked, and, behold, <char style="add">[he had]</char> sackcloth there upon his flesh.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />Then he said, God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> do so and more also to me, if the head of Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char> the son of Shafat <char style="add">[He Has Judged]</char> shall stand on him this day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />But Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char> sat in his house, and the elders sat with him; and <char style="add">[the king]</char> sent a man from before him: but before the messenger came to him, he said to the elders, See you<char style="ord">2f</char> how this son of a murderer has sent to take away my head? look, when the messenger comes, shut the door, and hold him fast at the door: <char style="add">[is]</char> not the sound of his master’s feet behind him?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />And while he yet talked with them, behold, the messenger came down unto him: and he said, Behold, this evil <char style="add">[is]</char> of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; why should I wait for the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> any longer?</para>
  <chapter number="7" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Then Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char> said, Hear you<char style="ord">2f</char> the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, Tomorrow about this time <char style="add">[shall]</char> a measure of fine flour <char style="add">[be sold]</char> for a shekel, and two measures of barley for a shekel, in the gate of Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Then a lord on whose hand the king leaned answered the man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and said, Behold, <char style="add">[if]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> would make windows in heaven, might this thing be? And he said, Behold, you<char style="ord">i</char> shall see <char style="add">[it]</char> with your<char style="ord">i</char> eyes, but shall not eat of it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And there were four leprous men at the entering in of the gate: and they said one to another, Why sit we here until we die?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />If we say, We will enter into the city, then the famine <char style="add">[is]</char> in the city, and we shall die there: and if we sit still here, we die also. Now therefore come, and let us fall unto the host of the Aram <char style="add">[Syrians]</char>: if they save us alive, we shall live; and if they kill us, we shall only die.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And they rose up in the twilight, to go unto the camp of the Aram <char style="add">[Syrians]</char>: and when they were come to the uttermost part of the camp of Aram <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char>, behold, <char style="add">[there was]</char> no man there.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />For the Lord-Adonai <char style="pn">(The Father)</char> <char style="add">[greatest above all]</char> had made the host of the Aram <char style="add">[Syrians]</char> to hear a noise of chariots, and a noise of horses, <char style="add">[even]</char> the noise of a great host: and they said one to another, Wow!, the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> has hired against us the kings of the Hitti <char style="add">[Terrorists]</char>, and the kings of the Mitzri, to come upon us.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />For this reason they arose and fled in the twilight, and left their tents, and their horses, and their asses, even the camp as it <char style="add">[was]</char>, and fled for their lives.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And when these lepers came to the outskirts part of the camp, they went into one tent, and did eat and drink, and carried from there silver, and gold, and clothing, and went and hid <char style="add">[it]</char>; and came again, and entered into another tent, and carried from there <char style="add">[also]</char>, and went and hid <char style="add">[it]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Then they said one to another, We do not well: this day <char style="add">[is]</char> a day of good tidings, and we hold our peace: if we wait till the morning light, some evil will come upon us: now therefore come, that we may go and tell the king’s household.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />So they came and called unto the porter of the city: and they told them, saying, We came to the camp of the Aram <char style="add">[Syrians]</char>, and, behold, <char style="add">[there was]</char> no man there, neither voice of man, but horses tied, and asses tied, and the tents as they <char style="add">[were empty]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And he called the porters; and they told <char style="add">[it]</char> to the king’s house within.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And the king arose in the night, and said unto his servants, I will now show you what the Aram <char style="add">[Syrians]</char> have done to us. They know that we <char style="add">[be]</char> hungry; therefore are they gone out of the camp to hide themselves in the field, saying, When they come out of the city, we shall catch them alive, and get into the city.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And one of his servants answered and said, Let <char style="add">[some]</char> take, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, five of the horses that remain, which are left in the city, <char style="pn">(behold, they [are] as all the multitude of Yisra’el [He Holds Onto The Heel Of God] that are left in it: behold, [I say], they [are] even as all the multitude of the Yisra’eli’s that are consumed)</char> and let us send them out and see.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />They took therefore two chariot horses; and the king sent after the host of the Aram <char style="add">[Syrians]</char>, saying, Go and see.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And they went after them unto Yarden <char style="add">[Descender]</char>: and, to their amazement, all the way <char style="add">[was]</char> full of garments and vessels, which the Aram <char style="add">[Syrians]</char> had cast away in their haste. And the messengers returned, and told the king.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And the people went out, and spoiled the tents of the Aram <char style="add">[Syrians]</char>. So a measure of fine flour was <char style="add">[sold]</char> for a shekel, and two measures of barley for a shekel, according to the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And the king appointed that lord on whose hand he leaned to be in charge of the gate: and the people trampled him down in the gate, and he died, as the man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> had said he would, who spoke when the king came down to him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And it came to pass as the man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> had spoken to the king, saying, Two measures of barley for a shekel, and a measure of fine flour for a shekel, shall be tomorrow about this time in the gate of Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And that lord answered the man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and said, Now, behold, <char style="add">[if]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> should make windows in heaven, might such a thing be? And he said, Behold, you<char style="ord">i</char> shall see it with your<char style="ord">i</char> eyes, but shall not eat thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And so it fell out unto him: for the people trampled upon him in the gate, and he died.</para>
  <chapter number="8" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Then spoke Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char> unto the woman, whose son he had restored to life, saying, Arise, and go you<char style="ord">i</char> and your<char style="ord">i</char> household, and stay wherever you<char style="ord">i</char> can stay: for the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has called for a famine; and it shall also come upon the land seven years.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And the woman arose, and did after the saying of the man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>: and she went with her household, and detained <char style="pn">(held)</char> in the land of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> seven years.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And it came to pass at the seven years’ end, that the woman returned out of the land of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>: and she went forth to claim unto the king for her house and for her land.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And the king talked with Geichazi <char style="add">[valley of vision]</char> the servant of the man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, saying, Tell me, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, all the great things that Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char> has done.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And it came to pass, as he was telling the king how he had restored a dead body to life, that, behold, the woman, whose son he had restored to life, cried to the king for her house and for her land. And Geichazi <char style="add">[valley of vision]</char> said, My lord, O king, this <char style="add">[is]</char> the woman, and this <char style="add">[is]</char> her son, whom Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char> restored to life.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And when the king asked the woman, she told him. So the king appointed unto her a certain officer, saying, Restore all that <char style="add">[was]</char> hers, and all the fruits of the field since the day that she left the land, even until now.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char> came to Dammesek <char style="pn">(Damascus)</char> <char style="add">[silent is the sackcloth weaver]</char>; and Ben-Hadad <char style="add">[son of the (false god) Hadad]</char> the king of Aram <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char> was sick; and it was told him, saying, The man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> is come here.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And the king said unto Haza’el <char style="add">[one who sees God]</char>, Take a present in your<char style="ord">i</char> hand, and go, meet the man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and enquire of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> by him, saying, Shall I recover of this disease?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />So Haza’el <char style="add">[one who sees God]</char> went to meet him, and took a present with him, even of every good thing of Dammesek <char style="pn">(Damascus)</char> <char style="add">[silent is the sackcloth weaver]</char>, forty camels’ burden, and came and stood before him, and said, Your<char style="ord">1s</char> son Ben-Hadad [son of the <char style="pn">(false god)</char> Hadad] king of Aram <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char> has sent me to you<char style="ord">i</char>, saying, Shall I recover of this disease?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char> said unto him, Go, say unto him, you<char style="ord">i</char> may certainly recover: howbeit the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has showed me that he shall surely die.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And he settled his gaze on the man so long that he <char style="pn">(Haza’el)</char> was ashamed: and the man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> wept.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And Haza’el <char style="add">[one who sees God]</char> said, Why weep my lord? And he answered, Because I know the evil that you<char style="ord">i</char> will do unto the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: their strong holds will you<char style="ord">i</char> set on fire, and their young men will you<char style="ord">i</char> slay with the sword, and will dash their children, and rip up their women with child.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And Haza’el <char style="add">[one who sees God]</char> said, But what, <char style="add">[is]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> servant? a dog? that he should do this great thing? And Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char> answered, The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has showed me that you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[shall be]</char> king over Aram <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />So he departed from Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char>, and came to his master; who said to him, What said Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char> to you<char style="ord">i</char>? And he answered, He told me <char style="add">[that]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> should surely recover.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And it came to pass on the morrow, that he took a thick cloth, and dipped <char style="add">[it]</char> in water, and spread <char style="add">[it]</char> on his face, so that he died: and Haza’el <char style="add">[one who sees God]</char> reigned in his place.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And in the fifth year of Yoram <char style="add">[Yehovah is exalted]</char> the son of Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged] [being]</char> then king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, Y’horam <char style="add">[Yehovah is exalted]</char> the son of Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> began to reign.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Thirty and two years old was he when he began to reign; and he reigned eight years in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And he walked in the way of the kings of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, as did the house of Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char>: for the daughter of Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> was his wife: and he did evil in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Yet the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> would not destroy Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> for David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> his servant’s sake, as he promised him to give him always a light, <char style="add">[and]</char> to his children.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />In his days Edom <char style="add">[Red]</char> revolted from under the hand of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and made a king over themselves.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />So Yoram <char style="add">[Yehovah is exalted]</char> went over to Tza’ir <char style="add">[small]</char>, and all the chariots with him: and he rose by night, and struck the Edomi <char style="add">[red]</char> which compassed him about, and the captains of the chariots: and the people fled into their tents.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />Yet Edom <char style="add">[Red]</char> revolted from under the hand of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> unto this day. Then Livnah <char style="add">[Pavement]</char> revolted at the same time.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And the rest of the acts of Yoram <char style="add">[Yehovah is exalted]</char>, and all that he did, <char style="add">[are]</char> they not written in the book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And Yoram <char style="add">[Yehovah is exalted]</char> slept with his fathers, and was buried with his fathers in the city of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>: and Achazyah <char style="add">[Yehovah possesses]</char> his son reigned in his stead.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />In the twelfth year of Yoram <char style="add">[Yehovah is exalted]</char> the son of Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> did Achazyah <char style="add">[Yehovah possesses]</char> the son of Y’horam <char style="add">[Yehovah is exalted]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> begin to reign.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />Two and twenty years old <char style="add">[was]</char> Achazyah <char style="add">[Yehovah possesses]</char> when he began to reign; and he reigned one year in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>. And his mother’s name <char style="add">[was]</char> ‘Atalyahu <char style="add">[afflicted of the Lord]</char>, the daughter of ‘Omri <char style="add">[pupil of Yehovah]</char> king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And he walked in the way of the house of Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char>, and did evil in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, as <char style="add">[did]</char> the house of Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char>: for he <char style="add">[was]</char> the son in law of the house of Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And he went with Yoram <char style="add">[Yehovah is exalted]</char> the son of Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> to the war against Haza’el <char style="add">[one who sees God]</char> king of Aram <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char> in Ramot-Gil’ad <char style="add">[rocky region]</char>; and the Aram <char style="add">[Syrians]</char> wounded Yoram <char style="add">[Yehovah is exalted]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And king Yoram <char style="add">[Yehovah is exalted]</char> went back to be healed in Yizre’el <char style="add">[God Sows]</char> of the wounds which the Aram <char style="add">[Syrians]</char> had given him at Ramah <char style="add">[Hill]</char>, when he fought against Haza’el <char style="add">[one who sees God]</char> king of Aram <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char>. And Achazyah <char style="add">[Yehovah possesses]</char> the son of Y’horam <char style="add">[Yehovah is exalted]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> went down to see Yoram <char style="add">[Yehovah is exalted]</char> the son of Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> in Yizre’el <char style="add">[God Sows]</char>, because he was sick.</para>
  <chapter number="9" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char> the prophet called one of the children of the prophets, and said unto him, Gird up your<char style="ord">i</char> waist, and take this box of oil in your<char style="ord">i</char> hand, and go to Ramot-Gil’ad <char style="add">[rocky region]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And when you<char style="ord">i</char> come there, look out there for Yehu <char style="add">[Yehovah is He]</char> the son of Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> the son of Nimshi <char style="add">[rescued]</char>, and go in, and make him arise up from among his brethren, and carry him to an inner chamber;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Then take the box of oil, and pour <char style="add">[it]</char> on his head, and say, Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, I have anointed you<char style="ord">i</char> king over Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>. Then open the door, and flee, and wait not.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />So the young man, <char style="add">[even]</char> the young man the prophet, went to Ramot-Gil’ad <char style="add">[rocky region]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And when he came, behold, the captains of the host <char style="add">[were]</char> sitting; and he said, I have an errand to you<char style="ord">i</char>, O captain. And Yehu <char style="add">[Yehovah is He]</char> said, Unto which of us? And he said, To you<char style="ord">i</char>, O captain.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And he arose, and went into the house; and he poured the oil on his head, and said unto him, Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, I have anointed you<char style="ord">i</char> king over the people of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, <char style="add">[even]</char> over Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall strike the house of Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> master, that I may avenge the blood of my servants the prophets, and the blood of all the servants of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, at the hand of Izevel <char style="add">[Ba’al exalts]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />For the whole house of Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> shall perish: and I will cut off from Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> him that pisses against the wall, and him that is shut up and left in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And I will make the house of Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> like the house of Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> the son of N’vat <char style="add">[aspect]</char>, and like the house of Ba’sha <char style="add">[wicked]</char> the son of Achiyah <char style="add">[brother of Yehovah]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And the dogs shall eat Izevel <char style="add">[Ba’al exalts]</char> in the dumping-ground of Yizre’el <char style="add">[God Sows]</char>, and <char style="add">[there shall be]</char> none to bury <char style="add">[her]</char>. And he opened the door, and fled.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Then Yehu <char style="add">[Yehovah is He]</char> came forth to the servants of his lord: and <char style="add">[one]</char> said unto him, <char style="add">[Is]</char> all well? For what reason came this mad <char style="add">[fellow]</char> to you<char style="ord">i</char>? And he said unto them, You<char style="ord">2f</char> know the man, and his communication.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And they said, <char style="add">[It is]</char> not true; tell us now. And he said, Thus and thus spoke he to me, saying, Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, I have anointed you<char style="ord">i</char> king over Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Then they hasted, and took every man his garment, and put <char style="add">[it]</char> under him on the top of the stairs, and blew with trumpets, saying, Yehu <char style="add">[Yehovah is He]</char> is king.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />So Yehu <char style="add">[Yehovah is He]</char> the son of Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> the son of Nimshi <char style="add">[rescued]</char> conspired against Yoram <char style="add">[Yehovah is exalted]</char>. (Now Yoram <char style="add">[Yehovah is exalted]</char> had kept Ramot-Gil’ad <char style="add">[rocky region]</char>, he and all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, because of Haza’el <char style="add">[one who sees God]</char> king of Aram <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />But king Yoram <char style="add">[Yehovah is exalted]</char> was returned to be healed in Yizre’el <char style="add">[God Sows]</char> of the wounds which the Aram <char style="add">[Syrians]</char> had given him, when he fought with Haza’el <char style="add">[one who sees God]</char> king of Aram <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char>.) And Yehu <char style="add">[Yehovah is He]</char> said, If it be your minds, <char style="add">[then]</char> let none go forth <char style="add">[nor]</char> escape out of the city to go to tell <char style="add">[it]</char> in Yizre’el <char style="add">[God Sows]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />So Yehu <char style="add">[Yehovah is He]</char> rode in a chariot, and went to Yizre’el <char style="add">[God Sows]</char>; for Yoram <char style="add">[Yehovah is exalted]</char> lay there. And Achazyah <char style="add">[Yehovah possesses]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> was come down to see Yoram <char style="add">[Yehovah is exalted]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And there stood a watchman on the tower in Yizre’el <char style="add">[God Sows]</char>, and he spied the company of Yehu <char style="add">[Yehovah is He]</char> as he came, and said, I see a company. And Yoram <char style="add">[Yehovah is exalted]</char> said, Take an horseman, and send to meet them, and let him say, <char style="add">[Do you come in]</char> peace?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />So there went one on horseback to meet him, and said, Thus says the king, <char style="add">[Is it]</char> peace? And Yehu <char style="add">[Yehovah is He]</char> said, What have you<char style="ord">i</char> to do with peace? turn you<char style="ord">i</char> behind me. And the watchman explained <char style="pn">(to the king)</char>, saying, The messenger came to them, but he comes not again.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Then he sent out a second on horseback, which came to them, and said, Thus says the king, <char style="add">[Is it]</char> peace? And Yehu <char style="add">[Yehovah is He]</char> answered, What have you<char style="ord">i</char> to do with peace? turn you<char style="ord">i</char> behind me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And the watchman told, saying, He came even unto them, and comes not again: and the driving <char style="add">[is]</char> like the driving of Yehu <char style="add">[Yehovah is He]</char> the son of Nimshi <char style="add">[rescued]</char>; for he drives furiously.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And Yoram <char style="add">[Yehovah is exalted]</char> said, Make ready. And his chariot was made ready. And Yoram <char style="add">[Yehovah is exalted]</char> king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> and Achazyah <char style="add">[Yehovah possesses]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> went out, each in his chariot, and they went out against Yehu <char style="add">[Yehovah is He]</char>, and met him in the portion of Navot <char style="add">[fruits]</char> the Yizre’eli <char style="add">[God Sows]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And it came to pass, when Yoram <char style="add">[Yehovah is exalted]</char> saw Yehu <char style="add">[Yehovah is He]</char>, that he said, <char style="add">[Is it]</char> peace, Yehu <char style="add">[Yehovah is He]</char>? And he answered, What peace, so long as the cult prostitution of your<char style="ord">i</char> mother Izevel <char style="add">[Ba’al exalts]</char> and her witchcrafts <char style="add">[are so]</char> many?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And Yoram <char style="add">[Yehovah is exalted]</char> turned his hands, and fled, and said to Achazyah <char style="add">[Yehovah possesses]</char>, Treachery! O Achazyah <char style="add">[Yehovah possesses]</char>!</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And Yehu <char style="add">[Yehovah is He]</char> drew a bow with his full strength, and struck Y’horam <char style="add">[Yehovah is exalted]</char> between his arms, and the arrow went out at his heart, and he sunk down in his chariot.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />Then said <char style="add">[Yehu [Yehovah is He]]</char> to Bidkar <char style="add">[with a stab]</char> his captain, Pick him up, <char style="add">[and]</char> cast him in the portion of the field of Navot <char style="add">[fruits]</char> the Yizre’eli <char style="add">[God Sows]</char>: for remember how that, when I and you<char style="ord">i</char> rode together after Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> his father, the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> pronounced this sentence upon him;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />Surely I have seen yesterday the blood of Navot <char style="add">[fruits]</char>, and the blood of his sons, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; and I will pay you<char style="ord">i</char> back in this field, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>. Now therefore take <char style="add">[and]</char> cast him into the field <char style="add">[of ground]</char>, according to the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />But when Achazyah <char style="add">[Yehovah possesses]</char> the king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> saw <char style="add">[this]</char>, he fled by the way of the garden house. And Yehu <char style="add">[Yehovah is He]</char> followed after him, and said, Strike him also in the chariot. <char style="add">[And they did so]</char> at the going up to Gur <char style="add">[sojourning]</char>, which <char style="add">[is]</char> by Yivle’am <char style="add">[Devouring the People]</char>. And he fled to Megiddo <char style="add">[Place of Crowds]</char>, and died there.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And his servants carried him in a chariot to Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, and buried him in his sepulcher with his fathers in the city of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And in the eleventh year of Yoram <char style="add">[Yehovah is exalted]</char> the son of Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> began Achazyah <char style="add">[Yehovah possesses]</char> to reign over Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And when Yehu <char style="add">[Yehovah is He]</char> was come to Yizre’el <char style="add">[God Sows]</char>, Izevel <char style="add">[Ba’al exalts]</char> heard <char style="add">[of it]</char>; and she painted her face, and fixed her hair, and looked out the window.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And as Yehu <char style="add">[Yehovah is He]</char> entered in at the gate, she said, <char style="add">[Are you here in]</char> peace Zimri <char style="add">[My Music]</char>? who murdered his master?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />And he lifted up his face to the window, and said, Who <char style="add">[is]</char> on my side? who? And there looked out to him two <char style="add">[or]</char> three eunuchs.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />And he said, Throw her down. So they threw her down: and <char style="add">[some]</char> of her blood was sprinkled on the wall, and on the horses: and he trampled her under foot.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />And when he was come in, he did eat and drink, and said, Go, see now this cursed <char style="add">[woman]</char>, and bury her: for she <char style="add">[is]</char> a king’s daughter.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />And they went to bury her: but they found no more of her than the skull, and the feet, and the palms of <char style="add">[her]</char> hands.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />For this reason they came again, and told him. And he said, This <char style="add">[is]</char> the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, which he spoke by his servant Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char> the Tishbi <char style="add">[captivity]</char>, saying, In the portion of Yizre’el <char style="add">[God Sows]</char> shall dogs eat the flesh of Izevel <char style="add">[Ba’al exalts]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" />And the carcass of Izevel <char style="add">[Ba’al exalts]</char> shall be as dung upon the face of the field in the portion of Yizre’el <char style="add">[God Sows]</char>; <char style="add">[so]</char> that they shall not say, This <char style="add">[is]</char> Izevel <char style="add">[Ba’al exalts]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="10" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> had seventy sons in Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>. And Yehu <char style="add">[Yehovah is He]</char> wrote letters, and sent to Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>, unto the rulers of Yizre’el <char style="add">[God Sows]</char>, to the elders, and to them that brought up Ach’av’s <char style="add">[father’s brother] [children]</char>, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Now as soon as this letter comes to you, seeing your master’s sons <char style="add">[are]</char> with you, and <char style="add">[there are]</char> with you chariots and horses, a fenced city also, and armour;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Look even out the best and most suitable of your master’s sons, and set <char style="add">[him]</char> on his father’s throne, and fight for your master’s house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />But they were exceedingly afraid, and said, Behold, two kings stood not before him: how then shall we stand?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And he that <char style="add">[was]</char> over the house, and he that <char style="add">[was]</char> over the city, the elders also, and the bringers up <char style="add">[of the children]</char>, sent to Yehu <char style="add">[Yehovah is He]</char>, saying, We <char style="add">[are]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> servants, and will do all that you<char style="ord">i</char> shall bid us; we will not make any king: do you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[that which is]</char> good in your<char style="ord">i</char> eyes.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Then he wrote a letter the second time to them, saying, If you<char style="ord">2f</char> <char style="add">[be]</char> mine, and <char style="add">[if]</char> you<char style="ord">2f</char> will hearken unto my voice, take you<char style="ord">2f</char> the heads of the men your master’s sons, and come to me to Yizre’el <char style="add">[God Sows]</char> by tomorrow this time. Now the king’s sons, <char style="add">[being]</char> seventy persons, <char style="add">[were]</char> with the great men of the city, which brought them up.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And it came to pass, when the letter came to them, that they took the king’s sons, and killed seventy persons, and put their heads in baskets, and sent him <char style="add">[them]</char> to Yizre’el <char style="add">[God Sows]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And there came a messenger, and told him, saying, They have brought the heads of the king’s sons. And he said, Lay you<char style="ord">2f</char> them in two heaps at the entering in of the gate until the morning.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And it came to pass in the morning, that he went out, and stood, and said to all the people, You<char style="ord">2f</char> <char style="add">[be]</char> righteous: behold, I conspired against my master, and killed him: but who killed all these?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Know now that there shall fall unto the earth nothing of the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, which the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> spoke concerning the house of Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char>: for the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has done <char style="add">[that]</char> which he spoke by his servant Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />So Yehu <char style="add">[Yehovah is He]</char> killed all that remained of the house of Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> in Yizre’el <char style="add">[God Sows]</char>, and all his great men, and his relatives, and his priests, until he left him none remaining.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And he arose and departed, and came to Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>. <char style="add">[And]</char> as he <char style="add">[was]</char> at the shearing house in the way,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Yehu <char style="add">[Yehovah is He]</char> met with the brethren of Achazyah <char style="add">[Yehovah possesses]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and said, Who <char style="add">[are]</char> you<char style="ord">2f</char>? And they answered, We <char style="add">[are]</char> the brethren of Achazyah <char style="add">[Yehovah possesses]</char>; and we go down to salute the children of the king and the children of the queen.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And he said, Take them alive. And they took them alive, and killed them at the pit of the shearing house, <char style="add">[even]</char> two and forty men; neither left he any of them <char style="add">[alive]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And when he was departed there, he lighted on Y’honadav <char style="add">[Yehovah is willing]</char> the son of Rekhav <char style="add">[rider] [coming]</char> to meet him: and he saluted him, and said to him, Is your<char style="ord">i</char> heart right, as my heart <char style="add">[is]</char> with your<char style="ord">i</char> heart? And Y’honadav <char style="add">[Yehovah is willing]</char> answered, It is. If it be, give <char style="add">[me]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> hand. And he gave <char style="add">[him]</char> his hand; and he took him up to him into the chariot.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And he said, Come with me, and see my zeal for the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>. So they made him ride in his chariot.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And when he came to Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>, he killed all that remained unto Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> in Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>, till he had destroyed him, according to the saying of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, which he spoke to Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And Yehu <char style="add">[Yehovah is He]</char> gathered all the people together, and said unto them, Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> served Ba’al [lord (a false god)] a little; <char style="add">[but]</char> Yehu <char style="add">[Yehovah is He]</char> shall serve him much.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Now therefore call unto me all the prophets of Ba’al <char style="add">[lord (a false god)]</char>, all his servants, and all his priests; let none be wanting: for I have a great sacrifice <char style="add">[to do]</char> to Ba’al <char style="add">[lord (a false god)]</char>; whosoever shall be wanting, he shall not live. But Yehu <char style="add">[Yehovah is He]</char> did <char style="add">[it]</char> in subtlety, to the intent that he might destroy the worshippers of Ba’al <char style="add">[lord (a false god)]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And Yehu <char style="add">[Yehovah is He]</char> said, Proclaim a solemn assembly for Ba’al <char style="add">[lord (a false god)]</char>. And they proclaimed <char style="add">[it]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And Yehu <char style="add">[Yehovah is He]</char> sent through all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: and all the worshippers of Ba’al <char style="add">[lord (a false god)]</char> came, so that there was not a man left that came not. And they came into the house of Ba’al <char style="add">[lord (a false god)]</char>; and the house of Ba’al <char style="add">[lord (a false god)]</char> was full from one end to another.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And he said unto him that <char style="add">[was]</char> over the wardrobe, Bring forth robes for all the worshippers of Ba’al <char style="add">[lord (a false god)]</char>. And he brought them forth robes.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And Yehu <char style="add">[Yehovah is He]</char> went, and Y’honadav <char style="add">[Yehovah is willing]</char> the son of Rekhav <char style="add">[rider]</char>, into the house of Ba’al <char style="add">[lord (a false god)]</char>, and said unto the worshippers of Ba’al <char style="add">[lord (a false god)]</char>, Search, and look that there be here with you none of the servants of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, but the worshippers of Ba’al <char style="add">[lord (a false god)]</char> only.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And when they went in to offer sacrifices and burnt offerings, Yehu <char style="add">[Yehovah is He]</char> appointed eighty men without, and said, <char style="add">[If]</char> any of the men whom I have brought into your hands escape, <char style="add">[he that lets him go]</char>, his life <char style="add">[shall be]</char> for the life of him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And it came to pass, as soon as he had made an end of offering the burnt offering, that Yehu <char style="add">[Yehovah is He]</char> said to the guard and to the captains, Go in, <char style="add">[and]</char> slay them; let none come forth. And they struck them with the edge of the sword; and the guard and the captains cast <char style="add">[them]</char> out, and went to the city of the house of Ba’al <char style="add">[lord (a false god)]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And they brought forth the images out of the house of Ba’al <char style="add">[lord (a false god)]</char>, and burned them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And they broke down the image of Ba’al <char style="add">[lord (a false god)]</char>, and broke down the house of Ba’al <char style="add">[lord (a false god)]</char>, and made it a latrine unto this day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />Thus Yehu <char style="add">[Yehovah is He]</char> destroyed Ba’al <char style="add">[lord (a false god)]</char> out of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />However <char style="add">[from]</char> the sins of Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> the son of N’vat <char style="add">[aspect]</char>, who made Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> to sin, Yehu <char style="add">[Yehovah is He]</char> departed not from after them, <char style="add">[that is to say]</char>, the golden calves that <char style="add">[were]</char> in Beit-El <char style="add">[House of God]</char>, and that <char style="add">[were]</char> in Dan <char style="add">[Judge]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto Yehu <char style="add">[Yehovah is He]</char>, Because you<char style="ord">i</char> have done well in executing <char style="add">[that which is]</char> right in my eyes, <char style="add">[and]</char> have done unto the house of Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> according to all that <char style="add">[was]</char> in my heart, your<char style="ord">i</char> children of the fourth <char style="add">[generation]</char> shall sit on the throne of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />But Yehu <char style="add">[Yehovah is He]</char> took no heed to walk in the law of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> with all his heart: for he departed not from the sins of Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char>, which made Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> to sin.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />In those days the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> began to cut Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> short: and Haza’el <char style="add">[one who sees God]</char> struck them in all the coasts of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />From Yarden <char style="add">[Descender]</char> eastward, all the land of Gil’ad <char style="add">[Rocky Region]</char>, the Gadi <char style="add">[my fortune] [A Troop]</char>, and the Re’uveni <char style="add">[behold, a son!]</char>, and the M’nasheh <char style="add">[Causing to Forget]</char>, from ‘Aeo’er <char style="add">[Ruins]</char>, which <char style="add">[is]</char> by the river ‘Arnon <char style="add">[Rushing Stream]</char>, even Gil’ad <char style="add">[Rocky Region]</char> and Bashan <char style="add">[Fruitful]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />Now the rest of the acts of Yehu <char style="add">[Yehovah is He]</char>, and all that he did, and all his might, <char style="add">[are]</char> they not written in the book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />And Yehu <char style="add">[Yehovah is He]</char> slept with his fathers: and they buried him in Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>. And Y’ho’achaz <char style="add">[Yehovah has seized]</char> his son reigned in his stead.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />And the time that Yehu <char style="add">[Yehovah is He]</char> reigned over Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> in Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain] [was]</char> twenty and eight years.</para>
  <chapter number="11" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And when ‘Atalyahu <char style="add">[afflicted of the Lord]</char> the mother of Achazyah <char style="add">[Yehovah possesses]</char> saw that her son was dead, she arose and destroyed all the seed royal.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />But Y’hosheva <char style="add">[Yehovah has sworn]</char>, the daughter of king Yoram <char style="add">[Yehovah is exalted]</char>, sister of Achazyah <char style="add">[Yehovah possesses]</char>, took Yo’ash <char style="add">[Given by the Lord]</char> the son of Achazyah <char style="add">[Yehovah possesses]</char>, and stole him from among the king’s sons <char style="add">[which were]</char> slain; and they hid him, <char style="add">[even]</char> him and his nurse, in the bedchamber from ‘Atalyahu <char style="add">[afflicted of the Lord]</char>, so that he was not slain.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And he was with her hid in the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> six years. And ‘Atalyahu <char style="add">[afflicted of the Lord]</char> did reign over the land.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And the seventh year Y’hoyada <char style="add">[Yehovah knows]</char> sent and fetched the rulers over hundreds, with the captains and the guard, and brought them to him into the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and made a covenant with them, and took an oath of them in the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and showed them the king’s son.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And he commanded them, saying, This <char style="add">[is]</char> the thing that you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall do; A tles hird part of you that enter in on the Shabbat <char style="add">[Rest]</char> shall even be keepers of the watch of the king’s house;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And a third part <char style="add">[shall be]</char> at the gate of Sur <char style="add">[turning aside]</char>; and a third part at the gate behind the guard: so shall you<char style="ord">2f</char> keep the watch of the house, that it be not broken down.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And two parts of all you that go forth on the Shabbat <char style="add">[Rest]</char>, even they shall keep the watch of the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> about the king.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall compass <char style="pn">(go around, encircle; encompass)</char> the king round about, every man with his weapons in his hand: and he that comes within the ranges, let him be slain: and be you<char style="ord">2f</char> with the king as he goes out and as he comes in.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And the captains over the hundreds did according to all <char style="add">[things]</char> that Y’hoyada <char style="add">[Yehovah knows]</char> the priest commanded: and they took every man his men that were to come in on the Shabbat <char style="add">[Rest]</char>, with them that should go out on the Shabbat <char style="add">[Rest]</char>, and came to Y’hoyada <char style="add">[Yehovah knows]</char> the priest.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And to the captains over hundreds did the priest give king David’s <char style="add">[beloved]</char>’s spears and shields, that <char style="add">[were]</char> in the temple of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And the guard stood, every man with his weapons in his hand, round about the king, from the right corner of the temple to the left corner of the temple, <char style="add">[along]</char> by the altar and the temple.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And he brought forth the king’s son, and put the crown upon him, and <char style="add">[gave him]</char> the testimony; and they made him king, and anointed him; and they clapped their hands, and said, Long live the king!</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And when ‘Atalyahu <char style="add">[afflicted of the Lord]</char> heard the noise of the guard <char style="add">[and]</char> of the people, she came to the people into the temple of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And when she looked, behold, the king stood by a pillar, as the custom <char style="add">[was]</char>, and the princes and the trumpeters by the king, and all the people of the land rejoiced, and blew with trumpets: and ‘Atalyahu <char style="add">[afflicted of the Lord]</char> rent her clothes, and cried, Treason, Treason!</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />But Y’hoyada <char style="add">[Yehovah knows]</char> the priest commanded the captains of the hundreds, the officers of the host, and said unto them, Bring her forth out past the ranks <char style="add">[of guards]</char>: and him that follows her kill with the sword. For the priest had said, Let her not be slain in the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And they laid hands on her; and she went by the way by the which the horses came into the king’s house: and there was she slain.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And Y’hoyada <char style="add">[Yehovah knows]</char> made a covenant between the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> and the king and the people, that they should be the LORD-Yehōvah’s <char style="add">[Messiah Pre-Incarnate]</char> people; between the king also and the people.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And all the people of the land went into the house of Ba’al <char style="add">[lord (a false god)]</char>, and broke it down; his altars and his images broke they in pieces thoroughly, and killed Mattan <char style="add">[a gift]</char> the priest of Ba’al <char style="add">[lord (a false god)]</char> before the altars. And the priest appointed officers over the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And he took the rulers over hundreds, and the captains, and the guard, and all the people of the land; and they brought down the king from the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and came by the way of the gate of the guard to the king’s house. And he sat on the throne of the kings.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And all the people of the land rejoiced, and the city was in quiet: and they killed ‘Atalyahu <char style="add">[afflicted of the Lord]</char> with the sword <char style="add">[beside]</char> the king’s house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />Seven years old <char style="add">[was]</char> Y’ho’ash <char style="add">[given by the Lord]</char> when he began to reign.</para>
  <chapter number="12" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />In the seventh year of Yehu <char style="add">[Yehovah is He]</char> Y’ho’ash <char style="add">[given by the Lord]</char> began to reign; and forty years reigned he in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>. And his mother’s name <char style="add">[was]</char> Tzivyah <char style="add">[roe]</char> of Be’er-sheva <char style="add">[Well of the sevenfold Oath]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And Y’ho’ash <char style="add">[given by the Lord]</char> did <char style="add">[that which was]</char> right in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> all his days wherein Y’hoyada <char style="add">[Yehovah knows]</char> the priest instructed him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />But the high places were not taken away: the people still sacrificed and burnt incense in the high places.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And Y’ho’ash <char style="add">[given by the Lord]</char> said to the priests, All the money of the dedicated things that is brought into the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, <char style="add">[even]</char> the money of everyone that passes <char style="add">[the account]</char>, the money that every man is set at, <char style="add">[and]</char> all the money that comes into any man’s heart to bring into the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Let the priests take <char style="add">[it]</char> to them, every man of his acquaintance: and let them repair the breaches of the house, wherever any breach <char style="pn">(breaking forth; a break; opening, inlet)</char> shall be found.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />But it was <char style="add">[so, that]</char> in the three and twentieth year of king Y’ho’ash <char style="add">[given by the Lord]</char> the priests had not repaired the breaches of the house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Then king Y’ho’ash <char style="add">[given by the Lord]</char> called for Y’hoyada <char style="add">[Yehovah knows]</char> the priest, and the <char style="add">[other]</char> priests, and said unto them, Why repair you<char style="ord">2f</char> not the breaches of the house? now therefore receive no <char style="add">[more]</char> money of those who contribute personally to you, but deliver it for the breaches of the house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And the priests consented to receive no <char style="add">[more]</char> money of the people, neither to repair the breaches of the house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />But Y’hoyada <char style="add">[Yehovah knows]</char> the priest took a chest, and bored a hole in the lid of it, and set it beside the altar, on the right side as one comes into the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: and the priests that kept the door put in it all the money <char style="add">[that was]</char> brought into the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And it was <char style="add">[so]</char>, when they saw that <char style="add">[there was]</char> much money in the chest, that the king’s scribe and the High Priest came up, and they put up in bags, and told the money that was found in the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And they gave the money, being told, into the hands of them that did the work, that had the oversight of the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: and they laid it out to the carpenters and builders, that worked upon the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And to masons, and hewers of stone, and to buy timber and hewed stone to repair the breaches of the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and for all that was laid out for the house to repair <char style="add">[it]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />However there were not made for the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> bowls of silver, snuffers, basons, trumpets, any vessels of gold, or vessels of silver, of the money <char style="add">[that was]</char> brought into the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />But they gave that to the workmen, and repaired with that the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Moreover they did not require and accounting with the men, into whose hand they delivered the money to be given to the workmen: for they dealt honestly.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />The trespass money and sin money was not brought into the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: it belonged to the priests’.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Then Haza’el <char style="add">[one who sees God]</char> king of Aram <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char> went up, and fought against Gat <char style="add">[Winepress]</char>, and took it: and Haza’el <char style="add">[one who sees God]</char> set his face to go up to Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And Y’ho’ash <char style="add">[given by the Lord]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> took all the consecrated things that Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char>, and Y’horam <char style="add">[Yehovah is exalted]</char>, and Achazyah <char style="add">[Yehovah possesses]</char>, his fathers, kings of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, had dedicated, and his own consecrated things, and all the gold <char style="add">[that was]</char> found in the treasures of the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and in the king’s house, and sent <char style="add">[it]</char> to Haza’el <char style="add">[one who sees God]</char> king of Aram <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char>: and he went away from Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And the rest of the acts of Yo’ash <char style="add">[Given by the Lord]</char>, and all that he did, <char style="add">[are]</char> they not written in the book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And his servants arose, and made a conspiracy, and killed Yo’ash <char style="add">[Given by the Lord]</char> in the Beit-Millo <char style="add">[fortification (defensive structure) or mound] [House of the Fortification (defensive structure)]</char>, which goes down to Sila <char style="add">[a highway]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />For Yozakhar <char style="add">[Yehovah remembers]</char> the son of Shim’at <char style="add">[report]</char>, and Y’hozavad <char style="add">[Yehovah has endowed]</char> the son of Shomer <char style="add">[keeper]</char>, his servants, struck him, and he died; and they buried him with his fathers in the city of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>: and Amatzyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is mighty]</char> his son reigned in his stead.</para>
  <chapter number="13" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />In the three and twentieth year of Yo’ash <char style="add">[Given by the Lord]</char> the son of Achazyah <char style="add">[Yehovah possesses]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> Y’ho’achaz <char style="add">[Yehovah has seized]</char> the son of Yehu <char style="add">[Yehovah is He]</char> began to reign over Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> in Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>, <char style="add">[and reigned]</char> seventeen years.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And he did <char style="add">[that which was]</char> evil in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and followed the sins of Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> the son of N’vat <char style="add">[aspect]</char>, which made Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> to sin; he departed not from them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And the anger of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> was kindled against Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and he delivered them into the hand of Haza’el <char style="add">[one who sees God]</char> king of Aram <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char>, and into the hand of Ben-Hadad [son of the <char style="pn">(false god)</char> Hadad] the son of Haza’el <char style="add">[one who sees God]</char>, all <char style="add">[their]</char> days.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And Y’ho’achaz <char style="add">[Yehovah has seized]</char> besought the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> listened unto him: for he saw the oppression of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, because the king of Aram <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char> oppressed them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />(And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> gave Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> a saviour, so that they went out from under the hand of the Aram <char style="add">[Syrians]</char>: and the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> dwelt in their tents, as formerly.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Nevertheless they departed not from the sins of the house of Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char>, who made Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> sin, <char style="add">[but]</char> walked in it: and there remained the grove also in Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>.)</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Neither did he leave of the people to Y’ho’achaz <char style="add">[Yehovah has seized]</char> but only fifty horsemen, and ten chariots, and ten thousand footmen; for the king of Aram <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char> had destroyed them, and had made them like the dust by threshing.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Now the rest of the acts of Y’ho’achaz <char style="add">[Yehovah has seized]</char>, and all that he did, and his might, <char style="add">[are]</char> they not written in the book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And Y’ho’achaz <char style="add">[Yehovah has seized]</char> slept with his fathers; and they buried him in Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>: and Yo’ash <char style="add">[Given by the Lord]</char> his son reigned in his place.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />In the thirty and seventh year of Yo’ash <char style="add">[Given by the Lord]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> began Y’ho’ash <char style="add">[given by the Lord]</char> the son of Y’ho’achaz <char style="add">[Yehovah has seized]</char> to reign over Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> in Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>, <char style="add">[and reigned]</char> sixteen years.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And he did <char style="add">[that which was]</char> evil in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; he departed not from all the sins of Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> the son of N’vat <char style="add">[aspect]</char>, who made Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> sin: <char style="add">[but]</char> he walked in it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And the rest of the acts of Yo’ash <char style="add">[Given by the Lord]</char>, and all that he did, and his might which he fought against Amatzyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is mighty]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, <char style="add">[are]</char> they not written in the book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And Yo’ash <char style="add">[Given by the Lord]</char> slept with his fathers; and Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> sat upon his throne: and Yo’ash <char style="add">[Given by the Lord]</char> was buried in Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char> with the kings of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Now Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char> was fallen sick of his sickness whereof he died. And Yo’ash <char style="add">[Given by the Lord]</char> the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> came down unto him, and wept over his face, and said, O my father, my father, the chariot of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and the horsemen thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char> said unto him, Take bow and arrows. And he took unto him bow and arrows.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And he said to the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, Put your<char style="ord">i</char> hand upon the bow. And he put his hand <char style="add">[upon it]</char>: and Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char> put his hands upon the king’s hands.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And he said, Open the window eastward. And he opened <char style="add">[it]</char>. Then Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char> said, Shoot. And he shot. And he said, The arrow of the LORD-Yehōvah’s <char style="add">[Messiah Pre-Incarnate]</char> deliverance, and the arrow of deliverance from Aram <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char>: for you<char style="ord">i</char> shall strike the Aram <char style="add">[Syrians]</char> in Aphek <char style="add">[Enclosure]</char>, till you<char style="ord">i</char> have consumed <char style="add">[them]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And he said, Take the arrows. And he took <char style="add">[them]</char>. And he said unto the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, Strike upon the ground. And he struck thrice, and stopped.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And the man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> was exceedingly angry with him, and said, you<char style="ord">i</char> should have smitten five or six times; then had you<char style="ord">i</char> smitten Aram <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char> till you<char style="ord">i</char> had consumed <char style="add">[it]</char>: whereas now you<char style="ord">i</char> shall strike Aram <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted] [but]</char> thrice.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char> died, and they buried him. And the bands of the Mo’avi <char style="add">[of his father]</char> invaded the land at the coming in of the year.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And it came to pass, as they were burying a man, that, behold, they spied a band <char style="add">[of men]</char>; and they cast the man into the sepulcher of Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char>: and when the man hinder <char style="pn">(or obstruct)</char> down, and touched the bones of Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char>, he revived, and stood up on his feet.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />But Haza’el <char style="add">[one who sees God]</char> king of Aram <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char> oppressed Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> all the days of Y’ho’achaz <char style="add">[Yehovah has seized]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> was gracious unto them, and had compassion on them, and had respect unto them, because of his covenant with Avraham <char style="add">[Exalted Father]</char>, Yitz’khak <char style="add">[Laughter]</char>, and Ya’akov <char style="add">[Heal of God]</char>, and would not destroy them, neither cast he them from his presence as yet.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />So Haza’el <char style="add">[one who sees God]</char> king of Aram <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char> died; and Ben-Hadad [son of the <char style="pn">(false god)</char> Hadad] his son reigned in his stead.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And Y’ho’ash <char style="add">[given by the Lord]</char> the son of Y’ho’achaz <char style="add">[Yehovah has seized]</char> took again out of the hand of Ben-Hadad <char style="add">[son of the (false god) Hadad]</char> the son of Haza’el <char style="add">[one who sees God]</char> the cities, which he had taken out of the hand of Y’ho’achaz <char style="add">[Yehovah has seized]</char> his father by war. Three times did Yo’ash <char style="add">[Given by the Lord]</char> beat him, and recovered the cities of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="14" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />In the second year of Yo’ash <char style="add">[Given by the Lord]</char> son of Y’ho’achaz <char style="add">[Yehovah has seized]</char> king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> reigned Amatzyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is mighty]</char> the son of Yo’ash <char style="add">[Given by the Lord]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />He was twenty and five years old when he began to reign, and reigned twenty and nine years in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>. And his mother’s name <char style="add">[was]</char> Y’ho’adan <char style="add">[Yehovah delights]</char> of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And he did <char style="add">[that which was]</char> right in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, yet not like David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> his father: he did according to all things as Yo’ash <char style="add">[Given by the Lord]</char> his father did.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />However the high places were not taken away: as yet the people did sacrifice and burnt incense on the high places.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And it came to pass, as soon as the kingdom was confirmed in his hand, that he killed his servants which had slain the king his father.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />But the children of the murderers he killed not: according unto that which is written in the book of the law of Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, wherein the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> commanded, saying, The fathers shall not be put to death for the children, nor the children be put to death for the fathers; but every man shall be put to death for his own sin.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />He killed of Edom <char style="add">[Red]</char> in the Valley of Salt ten thousand, and took Sela <char style="add">[the rocks] [the rock]</char> by war, and called the name of it Yokte’el <char style="add">[The Blessedness of God]</char> unto this day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Then Amatzyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is mighty]</char> sent messengers to Y’ho’ash <char style="add">[given by the Lord]</char>, the son of Y’ho’achaz <char style="add">[Yehovah has seized]</char> son of Yehu <char style="add">[Yehovah is He]</char>, king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, saying, Come, let us look one another in the face.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And Y’ho’ash <char style="add">[given by the Lord]</char> the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> sent to Amatzyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is mighty]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, saying, The thistle that <char style="add">[was]</char> in L’vanon <char style="add">[Whiteness]</char> sent to the cedar that <char style="add">[was]</char> in L’vanon <char style="add">[Whiteness]</char>, saying, Give your<char style="ord">i</char> daughter to my son to wife: and there passed by a wild beast that <char style="add">[was]</char> in L’vanon <char style="add">[Whiteness]</char>, and trampled down the thistle.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> have indeed smitten Edom <char style="add">[Red]</char>, and your<char style="ord">i</char> heart has lifted you<char style="ord">i</char> up: glory <char style="add">[of this]</char>, and wait at home: for why should you<char style="ord">i</char> meddle to <char style="add">[your<char style="ord">i</char>]</char> hurt, that you<char style="ord">i</char> should fall, <char style="add">[even]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char>, and Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> with you<char style="ord">i</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />But Amatzyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is mighty]</char> would not hear. Therefore Y’ho’ash <char style="add">[given by the Lord]</char> king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> went up; and he and Amatzyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is mighty]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> looked one another in the face at Beit-Shemesh <char style="add">[House of the Sun]</char>, which <char style="add">[belongs]</char> to Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> was put to the worse before Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>; and they fled every man to their tents.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And Y’ho’ash <char style="add">[given by the Lord]</char> king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> took Amatzyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is mighty]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, the son of Y’ho’ash <char style="add">[given by the Lord]</char> the son of Achazyah <char style="add">[Yehovah possesses]</char>, at Beit-Shemesh <char style="add">[House of the Sun]</char>, and came to Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, and broke down the wall of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> from the gate of Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char> unto the corner gate, six hundred feet long.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And he took all the gold and silver, and all the vessels that were found in the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and in the treasures of the king’s house, and hostages, and returned to Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Now the rest of the acts of Y’ho’ash <char style="add">[given by the Lord]</char> which he did, and his might, and how he fought with Amatzyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is mighty]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, <char style="add">[are]</char> they not written in the book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And Y’ho’ash <char style="add">[given by the Lord]</char> slept with his fathers, and was buried in Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char> with the kings of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>; and Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> his son reigned in his stead.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And Amatzyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is mighty]</char> the son of Yo’ash <char style="add">[Given by the Lord]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> lived after the death of Y’ho’ash <char style="add">[given by the Lord]</char> son of Y’ho’achaz <char style="add">[Yehovah has seized]</char> king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> fifteen years.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And the rest of the acts of Amatzyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is mighty]</char>, <char style="add">[are]</char> they not written in the book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Now they made a conspiracy against him in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>: and he fled to Lakhish <char style="add">[Invincible]</char>; but they sent after him to Lakhish <char style="add">[Invincible]</char>, and killed him there.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And they brought him on horses: and he was buried at Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> with his fathers in the city of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And all the people of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> took ‘Azaryah <char style="add">[Yehovah has helped]</char>, which <char style="add">[was]</char> sixteen years old, and made him king instead of his father Amatzyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is mighty]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />He built Eilat <char style="add">[Grove of Lofty Trees]</char>, and restored it to Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, after that the king slept with his fathers.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />In the fifteenth year of Amatzyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is mighty]</char> the son of Yo’ash <char style="add">[Given by the Lord]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> the son of Yo’ash <char style="add">[Given by the Lord]</char> king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> began to reign in Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>, <char style="add">[and reigned]</char> forty and one years.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And he did <char style="add">[that which was]</char> evil in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: he departed not from all the sins of Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> the son of N’vat <char style="add">[aspect]</char>, who made Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> to sin.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />He restored the coast of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> from the entering of Hamat <char style="add">[Fortress]</char> unto the sea of the plain, according to the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, which he spoke by the hand of his servant Yonah <char style="add">[dove]</char>, the son of Amitai <char style="add">[my truth]</char>, the prophet, which <char style="add">[was]</char> of Gat-Hefer <char style="add">[the winepress of digging]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />For the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> saw the affliction of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, <char style="add">[that it was]</char> very bitter: for <char style="add">[there was]</char> not any shut up, nor any left, nor any helper for Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said not that he would blot out the name of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> from under heaven: but he saved them by the hand of Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> the son of Yo’ash <char style="add">[Given by the Lord]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />Now the rest of the acts of Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char>, and all that he did, and his might, how he warred, and how he recovered Dammesek <char style="pn">(Damascus)</char> <char style="add">[silent is the sackcloth weaver]</char>, and Hamat <char style="add">[Fortress]</char>, <char style="add">[which belonged]</char> to Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, for Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, are they not written in the book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> slept with his fathers, <char style="add">[even]</char> with the kings of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>; and Z’kharyah <char style="add">[Yehovah remembers] [the Lord recalled]</char> his son reigned in his place.</para>
  <chapter number="15" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />In the twenty and seventh year of Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> began ‘Azaryah <char style="add">[Yehovah has helped]</char> son of Amatzyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is mighty]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> to reign.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Sixteen years old was he when he began to reign, and he reigned two and fifty years in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>. And his mother’s name <char style="add">[was]</char> Y’kholyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is able]</char> of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And he did <char style="add">[that which was]</char> right in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, according to all that his father Amatzyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is mighty]</char> had done;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Save that the high places were not removed: the people sacrificed and burnt incense still on the high places.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> struck the king, so that he was a leper unto the day of his death, and dwelt in a separate house. And Toram <char style="add">[Yehovah is Perfect]</char> the king’s son <char style="add">[was]</char> over the house, <char style="add">[as regent]</char> judging the people of the land.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And the rest of the acts of ‘Azaryah <char style="add">[Yehovah has helped]</char>, and all that he did, <char style="add">[are]</char> they not written in the book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />So ‘Azaryah <char style="add">[Yehovah has helped]</char> slept with his fathers; and they buried him with his fathers in the city of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>: and Toram <char style="add">[Yehovah is Perfect]</char> his son reigned in his stead.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />In the thirty and eighth year of ‘Azaryah <char style="add">[Yehovah has helped]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> did Z’kharyah <char style="add">[Yehovah remembers] [the Lord recalled]</char> the son of Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> reign over Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> in Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char> six months.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And he did <char style="add">[that which was]</char> evil in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, as his fathers had done: he departed not from the sins of Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> the son of N’vat <char style="add">[aspect]</char>, who made Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> to sin.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And Shalum <char style="add">[retribution]</char> the son of Yavesh <char style="add">[dry]</char> conspired against him, and struck him before the people, and killed him, and reigned in his stead.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And the rest of the acts of Z’kharyah <char style="add">[Yehovah remembers] [the Lord recalled]</char>, behold, they <char style="add">[are]</char> written in the book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />This <char style="add">[was]</char> the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> which he spoke unto Yehu <char style="add">[Yehovah is He]</char>, saying, Your<char style="ord">1s</char> sons shall sit on the throne of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> unto the fourth <char style="add">[generation]</char>. And so it came to pass.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Shalum <char style="add">[retribution]</char> the son of Yavesh <char style="add">[dry]</char> began to reign in the nine and thirtieth year of ‘Uziyah <char style="add">[my strength is Yehovah]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>; and he reigned a full month in Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />For Menachem <char style="add">[comforter]</char> the son of Gadi <char style="add">[my fortune]</char> went up from Tirtzah <char style="add">[Favourable]</char>, and came to Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>, and struck Shalum <char style="add">[retribution]</char> the son of Yavesh <char style="add">[dry]</char> in Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>, and killed him, and reigned in his stead.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And the rest of the acts of Shalum <char style="add">[retribution]</char>, and his conspiracy which he made, behold, they <char style="add">[are]</char> written in the book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Then Menachem <char style="add">[comforter]</char> struck Tifsach <char style="add">[cross over]</char>, and all that <char style="add">[were]</char> in it, and the coasts thereof from Tirtzah <char style="add">[Favourable]</char>: because they opened not <char style="add">[their gates to him]</char>, therefore he struck <char style="add">[it; and]</char> all the women in it that were with child he ripped up.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />In the nine and thirtieth year of ‘Azaryah <char style="add">[Yehovah has helped]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> began Menachem <char style="add">[comforter]</char> the son of Gadi <char style="add">[my fortune]</char> to reign over Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, <char style="add">[and reigned]</char> ten years in Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And he did <char style="add">[that which was]</char> evil in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: he departed not all his days from the sins of Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> the son of N’vat <char style="add">[aspect]</char>, who made Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> to sin.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[And]</char> Pul <char style="add">[distinguishing]</char> the king of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char> came against the land: and Menachem <char style="add">[comforter]</char> gave Pul <char style="add">[distinguishing]</char> a thirty-three tons of silver, that his hand might be with him to confirm the kingdom in his hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And Menachem <char style="add">[comforter]</char> exacted the money of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, <char style="add">[even]</char> of all the mighty men of wealth, of each man fifty shekels of silver, to give to the king of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> (the land of the sons of Shem <char style="pn">(name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char>. So the king of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> (the land of the sons of Shem <char style="pn">(name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char> turned back, and detained <char style="pn">(held)</char> not there in the land.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And the rest of the acts of Menachem <char style="add">[comforter]</char>, and all that he did, <char style="add">[are]</char> they not written in the book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And Menachem <char style="add">[comforter]</char> slept with his fathers; and P’kachyah <char style="add">[Yehovah sees]</char> his son reigned in his place.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />In the fiftieth year of ‘Azaryah <char style="add">[Yehovah has helped]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> P’kachyah <char style="add">[Yehovah sees]</char> the son of Menachem <char style="add">[comforter]</char> began to reign over Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> in Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>, <char style="add">[and reigned]</char> two years.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And he did <char style="add">[that which was]</char> evil in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: he departed not from the sins of Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> the son of N’vat <char style="add">[aspect]</char>, who made Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> to sin.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />But Pekach <char style="add">[opened]</char> the son of Remalyahu <char style="add">[protected by Yehovah]</char>, a captain of his, conspired against him, and struck him in Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>, in the palace of the king’s house, with Argov <char style="add">[Heap of Clods]</char> and Aryeh <char style="add">[lion]</char>, and with him fifty men of the Gil’adi <char style="add">[son]</char>: and he killed him, and reigned in his room.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And the rest of the acts of P’kachyah <char style="add">[Yehovah sees]</char>, and all that he did, behold, they <char style="add">[are]</char> written in the book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />In the two and fiftieth year of ‘Azaryah <char style="add">[Yehovah has helped]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> Pekach <char style="add">[opened]</char> the son of Remalyahu <char style="add">[protected by Yehovah]</char> began to reign over Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> in Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>, <char style="add">[and reigned]</char> twenty years.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And he did <char style="add">[that which was]</char> evil in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: he departed not from the sins of Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> the son of N’vat <char style="add">[aspect]</char>, who made Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> to sin.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />In the days of Pekach <char style="add">[opened]</char> king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> came Tiglat-Pil’eser <char style="add">[you will uncover the wonderful bond]</char> king of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> (the land of the sons of Shem <char style="pn">(name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char>, and took ‘Iyon <char style="add">[a ruin]</char>, and Avel-Beit-Ma’akhah <char style="add">[meadow of the house of oppression]</char>, and Yanoach <char style="add">[He rests]</char>, and Kedesh <char style="add">[Holy Place]</char>, and Hatzor <char style="add">[Castle]</char>, and Gil’ad <char style="add">[Rocky Region]</char>, and Galil <char style="add">[circuit, district]</char>, all the land of Naftali <char style="add">[My Wrestling]</char>, and carried them captive to Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And Hoshea <char style="add">[salvation]</char> the son of Elah <char style="add">[an oak]</char> made a conspiracy against Pekach <char style="add">[opened]</char> the son of Remalyahu <char style="add">[protected by Yehovah]</char>, and struck him, and killed him, and reigned in his stead, in the twentieth year of Toram <char style="add">[Yehovah is Perfect]</char> the son of ‘Uziyah <char style="add">[my strength is Yehovah]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And the rest of the acts of Pekach <char style="add">[opened]</char>, and all that he did, behold, they <char style="add">[are]</char> written in the book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />In the second year of Pekach <char style="add">[opened]</char> the son of Remalyahu <char style="add">[protected by Yehovah]</char> king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> began Toram <char style="add">[Yehovah is Perfect]</char> the son of ‘Uziyah <char style="add">[my strength is Yehovah]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> to reign.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />Five and twenty years old was he when he began to reign, and he reigned sixteen years in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>. And his mother’s name <char style="add">[was]</char> Yerusha <char style="add">[dispossessor]</char>, the daughter of Tzadok <char style="add">[righteous]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />And he did <char style="add">[that which was]</char> right in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: he did according to all that his father ‘Uziyah <char style="add">[my strength is Yehovah]</char> had done.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />However the high places were not removed: the people sacrificed and burned incense still in the high places. He built the higher gate of the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />Now the rest of the acts of Toram <char style="add">[Yehovah is Perfect]</char>, and all that he did, <char style="add">[are]</char> they not written in the book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" />In those days the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> began to send against Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> Retzin <char style="add">[firm]</char> the king of Aram <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char>, and Pekach <char style="add">[opened]</char> the son of Remalyahu <char style="add">[protected by Yehovah]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" />And Toram <char style="add">[Yehovah is Perfect]</char> slept with his fathers, and was buried with his fathers in the city of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> his father: and Achaz <char style="add">[he has grasped]</char> his son reigned in his stead.</para>
  <chapter number="16" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />In the seventeenth year of Pekach <char style="add">[opened]</char> the son of Remalyahu <char style="add">[protected by Yehovah]</char> Achaz <char style="add">[he has grasped]</char> the son of Toram <char style="add">[Yehovah is Perfect]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> began to reign.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Twenty years old <char style="add">[was]</char> Achaz <char style="add">[he has grasped]</char> when he began to reign, and reigned sixteen years in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, and did not <char style="add">[that which was]</char> right in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> his God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, like David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> his father.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />But he walked in the way of the kings of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, not only this but even made his son to pass through the fire, according to the abominations of the heathen, whom the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> cast out from before the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And he sacrificed and burnt incense in the high places, and on the hills, and under every green tree.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Then Retzin <char style="add">[firm]</char> king of Aram <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char> and Pekach <char style="add">[opened]</char> son of Remalyahu <char style="add">[protected by Yehovah]</char> king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> came up to Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> to war: and they besieged Achaz <char style="add">[he has grasped]</char>, but could not overcome <char style="add">[him]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />At that time Retzin <char style="add">[firm]</char> king of Aram <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char> recovered Eilat <char style="add">[Grove of Lofty Trees]</char> to Aram <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char>, and drove the Y’hudim <char style="pn">(Judeans)</char> from Eilat <char style="add">[Grove of Lofty Trees]</char>: and the Aram <char style="add">[Syrians]</char> came to Eilat <char style="add">[Grove of Lofty Trees]</char>, and dwelt there unto this day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />So Achaz <char style="add">[he has grasped]</char> sent messengers to Tiglat-Pil’eser <char style="add">[you will uncover the wonderful bond]</char> king of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> (the land of the sons of Shem <char style="pn">(name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char>, saying, I <char style="add">[am]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> servant and your<char style="ord">i</char> son: come up, and save me out of the hand of the king of Aram <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char>, and out of the hand of the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, which rise up against me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And Achaz <char style="add">[he has grasped]</char> took the silver and gold that was found in the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and in the treasures of the king’s house, and sent <char style="add">[it for]</char> a present to the king of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And the king of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char> listened unto him: for the king of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> (the land of the sons of Shem <char style="pn">(name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char> went up against Dammesek <char style="pn">(Damascus)</char> <char style="add">[silent is the sackcloth weaver]</char>, and took it, and carried <char style="add">[the people of]</char> it captive to Kir <char style="add">[wall]</char>, and killed Retzin <char style="add">[firm]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And king Achaz <char style="add">[he has grasped]</char> went to Dammesek <char style="pn">(Damascus)</char> <char style="add">[silent is the sackcloth weaver]</char> to meet Tiglat-Pil’eser <char style="add">[you will uncover the wonderful bond]</char> king of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char>, and saw an altar that <char style="add">[was]</char> at Dammesek <char style="pn">(Damascus)</char> <char style="add">[silent is the sackcloth weaver]</char>: and king Achaz <char style="add">[he has grasped]</char> sent to Uriyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is my flame]</char> the priest the fashion of the altar, and the pattern of it, according to all the workmanship thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And Uriyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is my flame]</char> the priest built an altar according to all that king Achaz <char style="add">[he has grasped]</char> had sent from Dammesek <char style="pn">(Damascus)</char> <char style="add">[silent is the sackcloth weaver]</char>: so Uriyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is my flame]</char> the priest made <char style="add">[it]</char> against king Achaz <char style="add">[he has grasped]</char> came from Dammesek <char style="pn">(Damascus)</char> <char style="add">[silent is the sackcloth weaver]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And when the king was come from Dammesek <char style="pn">(Damascus)</char> <char style="add">[silent is the sackcloth weaver]</char>, the king saw the altar: and the king approached to the altar, and offered thereon.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And he burnt his burnt offering and his meat offering, and poured his drink offering, and sprinkled the blood of his peace offerings, upon the altar.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And he brought also the brazen altar, which <char style="add">[was]</char> before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, from the forefront of the house, from between the altar and the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and put it on the north side of the altar.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And king Achaz <char style="add">[he has grasped]</char> commanded Uriyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is my flame]</char> the priest, saying, Upon the great altar burn the morning burnt offering, and the evening meat offering, and the king’s burnt sacrifice, and his meat offering, with the burnt offering of all the people of the land, and their meat offering, and their drink offerings; and sprinkle upon it all the blood of the burnt offering, and all the blood of the sacrifice: and the brazen altar shall be for me to enquire <char style="add">[by]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Thus did Uriyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is my flame]</char> the priest, according to all that king Achaz <char style="add">[he has grasped]</char> commanded.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And king Achaz <char style="add">[he has grasped]</char> cut off the borders of the bases, and removed the Wash basin from off them; and took down the sea from off the brazen oxen that <char style="add">[were]</char> under it, and put it upon a pavement of stones.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And the colonnade for the Shabbat <char style="add">[Rest]</char> that they had built in the house, and the king’s entry without, turned he from the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> for the king of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Now the rest of the acts of Achaz <char style="add">[he has grasped]</char> which he did, <char style="add">[are]</char> they not written in the book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And Achaz <char style="add">[he has grasped]</char> slept with his fathers, and was buried with his fathers in the city of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>: and Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> his son reigned in his stead.</para>
  <chapter number="17" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />In the twelfth year of Achaz <char style="add">[he has grasped]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> began Hoshea <char style="add">[salvation]</char> the son of Elah <char style="add">[an oak]</char> to reign in Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char> over Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> nine years.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And he did <char style="add">[that which was]</char> evil in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, but not as the kings of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> that were before him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Against him came up Shalman’eser <char style="add">[fire-worshipper] [fire-worshipper]</char> king of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> (the land of the sons of Shem (name, renown <char style="pn">(great reputation; being well-known)))</char>; and Hoshea <char style="add">[salvation]</char> became his servant, and gave him presents.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And the king of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char> found conspiracy in Hoshea <char style="add">[salvation]</char>: for he had sent messengers to So <char style="add">[concealed]</char> king of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, and brought no present to the king of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char>, as <char style="add">[he had done]</char> year by year: therefore the king of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char> shut him up, and bound him in prison.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Then the king of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char> came up throughout all the land, and went up to Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>, and besieged it three years.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />In the ninth year of Hoshea <char style="add">[salvation]</char> the king of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char> took Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>, and carried Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> away into Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char>, and placed them in Halach <char style="add">[painful]</char> and in Havor <char style="add">[joining] [by]</char> the river of Gozan <char style="add">[a cutting off]</char>, and in the cities of the Medes <char style="add">[middle land]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />For <char style="add">[so]</char> it was, that the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> had sinned against the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> their God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, which had brought them up out of the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, from under the hand of Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> king of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, and had feared other gods,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And walked in the statutes of the heathen, whom the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> cast out from before the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and of the kings of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, which they had made.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> did secretly <char style="add">[those]</char> things that <char style="add">[were]</char> not right against the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> their God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and they built them high places in all their cities, from the tower of the watchmen to the fenced city.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And they set them up images and groves in every high hill, and under every green tree:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And there they burnt incense in all the high places, as <char style="add">[did]</char> the heathen whom the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> carried away before them; and wrought wicked things to provoke the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> to anger:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />For they served idols, whereof the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had said unto them, You<char style="ord">2f</char> shall not do this thing.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Yet the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> testified against Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and against Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, by all the prophets, <char style="add">[and by]</char> all the seers, saying, Turn you<char style="ord">2f</char> from your evil ways, and keep my commandments <char style="add">[and]</char> my statutes, according to all the law which I commanded your fathers, and which I sent to you by my servants the prophets.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Yet they would not hear, but hardened their necks, like to the neck of their fathers, that did not believe in the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> their God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And they rejected his statutes, and his covenant that he made with their fathers, and his testimonies which he testified against them; and they followed vanity, and became vain, and went after the heathen that <char style="add">[were]</char> round about them, <char style="add">[concerning]</char> whom the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had charged them, that they should not do like them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And they left all the commandments of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> their God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and made them molten images, <char style="add">[even]</char> two calves, and made a grove, and worshipped all the army of heaven, and served Ba’al <char style="add">[lord (a false god)]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And they caused their sons and their daughters to pass through the fire, and used divination and enchantments, and sold themselves to do evil in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, to provoke him to anger.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Therefore the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> was very angry with Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and removed them out of his sight: there was none left but the tribe of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> only.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Also Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> kept not the commandments of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> their God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, but walked in the statutes of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> which they made.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> rejected all the seed of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and afflicted them, and delivered them into the hand of spoilers, until he had cast them out of his sight.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />For he rent Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> from the house of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>; and they made Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> the son of N’vat <char style="add">[aspect]</char> king: and Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> drove Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> from following the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and made them sin a great sin.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />For the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> walked in all the sins of Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> which he did; they departed not from them;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />Until the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> removed Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> out of his sight, as he had said by all his servants the prophets. So was Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> carried away out of their own land to Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char> unto this day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And the king of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char> brought <char style="add">[men]</char> from Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char>, and from Kutah <char style="add">[crushing]</char>, and from ‘Ava <char style="add">[ruin]</char>, and from Hamat <char style="add">[Fortress]</char>, and from S’farvayim <char style="add">[the two Sipparas (the city of books)]</char>, and placed <char style="add">[them]</char> in the cities of Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char> instead of the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: and they possessed Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>, and dwelt in the cities thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And <char style="add">[so]</char> it was at the beginning of their dwelling there, <char style="add">[that]</char> they feared not the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: therefore the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> sent lions among them, which killed <char style="add">[some]</char> of them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />For what reason they spoke to the king of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char>, saying, The nations which you<char style="ord">i</char> have removed, and placed in the cities of Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>, know not the manner of the God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of the land: therefore he has sent lions among them, and, behold, they slay them, because they know not the manner of the God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of the land.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />Then the king of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char> commanded, saying, Carry there one of the priests whom you<char style="ord">2f</char> brought from there; and let them go and dwell there, and let him teach them the manner of the God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of the land.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />Then one of the priests whom they had carried away from Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char> came and dwelt in Beit-El <char style="add">[House of God]</char>, and taught them how they should fear the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />However every nation made gods of their own, and put <char style="add">[them]</char> in the houses of the high places which the Shomronim [of Samaria (the watch-mountain)] had made, every nation in their cities wherein they dwelt.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And the men of Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char> made Sukkot-B’not <char style="add">[the daughter’s booth]</char>, and the men of Kutah <char style="add">[crushing]</char> made Nergal <char style="add">[hero]</char>, and the men of Hamat <char style="add">[Fortress]</char> made Ashima [guiltiness: I will make desolate],</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And the ‘Avim <char style="add">[Ruins]</char> made Nivchaz <char style="add">[the barker]</char> and Tartak <char style="add">[prince of darkness]</char>, and the S’farvim <char style="add">[enumeration]</char> burnt their children in fire to Adramelekh <char style="add">[honor of the king, or Adar is prince]</char> and Adramelekh <char style="add">[image of the king]</char>, the gods of S’farvayim <char style="add">[the two Sipparas (the city of books)]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />So they feared the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and made unto themselves of the lowest of them priests of the high places, which sacrificed for them in the houses of the high places.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />They feared the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and served their own gods, after the manner of the nations whom they carried away from there.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />Unto this day they do after the former manners: they fear not the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, neither do they after their statutes, or after their ordinances, or after the law and commandment which the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> commanded the children of Ya’akov <char style="add">[Heal of God]</char>, whom he named Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />With whom the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had made a covenant, and charged them, saying, You<char style="ord">2f</char> shall not fear other gods, nor bow yourselves to them, nor serve them, nor sacrifice to them:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />But the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, who brought you up out of the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> with great power and a stretched out arm, him shall you<char style="ord">2f</char> fear, and him shall you<char style="ord">2f</char> worship, and to him shall you<char style="ord">2f</char> do sacrifice.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" />And the statutes, and the ordinances, and the law, and the commandment, which he wrote for you, you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall observe to do forevermore; and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall not fear other gods.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" />And the covenant that I have made with you you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall not forget; neither shall you<char style="ord">2f</char> fear other gods.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" />But the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> your God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall fear; and he shall deliver you out of the hand of all your enemies.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="40" style="v" />However they did not hearken, but they did after their former manner.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="41" style="v" />So these nations feared the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and served their graven images, both their children, and their children’s children: as did their fathers, so do they unto this day.</para>
  <chapter number="18" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Now it came to pass in the third year of Hoshea <char style="add">[salvation]</char> son of Elah <char style="add">[an oak]</char> king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, <char style="add">[that]</char> Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> the son of Achaz <char style="add">[he has grasped]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> began to reign.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Twenty and five years old was he when he began to reign; and he reigned twenty and nine years in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>. His mother’s name also <char style="add">[was]</char> Avi <char style="add">[my father]</char>, the daughter of Z’kharyah <char style="add">[Yehovah remembers] [the Lord recalled]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And he did <char style="add">[that which was]</char> right in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, according to all that David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> his father did.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />He removed the high places, and broke the images, and cut down the groves, and broke in pieces the brazen serpent that Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> had made: for unto those days the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> did burn incense to it: and he called it N’chushtan <char style="add">[the bronze]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />He trusted in the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>; so that after him was none like him among all the kings of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, nor <char style="add">[any]</char> that were before him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />For he clave to the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, <char style="add">[and]</char> departed not from following him, but kept his commandments, which the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> commanded Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> was with him; <char style="add">[and]</char> he prospered to wherever he went forth: and he rebelled against the king of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char>, and served him not.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />He struck the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>, <char style="add">[even]</char> unto ‘Azah <char style="add">[The Strong]</char>, and the borders thereof, from the tower of the watchmen to the fenced city.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And it came to pass in the fourth year of king Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char>, which <char style="add">[was]</char> the seventh year of Hoshea <char style="add">[salvation]</char> son of Elah <char style="add">[an oak]</char> king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, <char style="add">[that]</char> Shalman’eser <char style="add">[fire-worshipper] [fire-worshipper]</char> king of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char> came up against Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>, and besieged it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And at the end of three years they took it: <char style="add">[even]</char> in the sixth year of Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char>, that <char style="add">[is]</char> the ninth year of Hoshea <char style="add">[salvation]</char> king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char> was taken.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And the king of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char> did carry away Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> unto Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char>, and put them in Halach <char style="add">[painful]</char> and in Havor <char style="add">[joining] [by]</char> the river of Gozan <char style="add">[a cutting off]</char>, and in the cities of the Medes <char style="add">[middle land]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Because they obeyed not the voice of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> their God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, but transgressed his covenant, <char style="add">[and]</char> all that Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> the servant of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> commanded, and would not hear <char style="add">[them]</char>, nor do <char style="add">[them]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Now in the fourteenth year of king Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> did Sancheriv <char style="add">[Sin (the moon) multiplied brothers]</char> king of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char> come up against all the fenced cities of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and took them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> sent to the king of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char> to Lakhish <char style="add">[Invincible]</char>, saying, I have offended; return from me: that which you<char style="ord">i</char> put on me will I bear. And the king of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char> appointed unto Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> three hundred talents of silver and thirty talents of gold.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> gave <char style="add">[him]</char> all the silver that was found in the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and in the treasures of the king’s house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />At that time did Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> cut off <char style="add">[the gold from]</char> the doors of the temple of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and <char style="add">[from]</char> the pillars which Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> had overlaid, and gave it to the king of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And the king of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char> sent Tartan <char style="add">[general]</char> and Rav-Saris <char style="add">[chief eunuch]</char> and Rav-Shakeh <char style="add">[chief cupbearer]</char> from Lakhish <char style="add">[Invincible]</char> to king Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> with a great host against Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>. And they went up and came to Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>. And when they were come up, they came and stood by the conduit of the upper pool, which <char style="add">[is]</char> in the highway of the Launderers’ Field.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And when they had called to the king, there came out to them Elyakim <char style="add">[God sets up]</char> the son of Hilkiyahu <char style="add">[my portion is Yehovah]</char>, which <char style="add">[was]</char> over the household, and Shevnah <char style="add">[vigour]</char> the scribe, and Yo’ach <char style="add">[Yahovah is brother]</char> the son of Asaf <char style="add">[gatherer]</char> the recorder.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And Rav-Shakeh <char style="add">[chief cupbearer]</char> said unto them, Speak you<char style="ord">2f</char> now to Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char>, Thus says the great king, the king of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char>, What confidence <char style="add">[is]</char> this wherein you<char style="ord">i</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />You<char style="ord">i</char> say, <char style="pn">(but [they are but] vain words,)</char> <char style="add">[I have]</char> counsel and strength for the war. Now on whom do you<char style="ord">i</char> trust, that you<char style="ord">i</char> rebel against me?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />Now, behold, you<char style="ord">i</char> trust upon the staff of this bruised reed, <char style="add">[even]</char> upon Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, on which if a man lean, it will go into his hand, and pierce it: so <char style="add">[is]</char> Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> king of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> unto all that trust on him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />But if you<char style="ord">2f</char> say unto me, We trust in the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> our God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>: <char style="add">[is]</char> not that he, whose high places and whose altars Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> has taken away, and has said to Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> and Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, You<char style="ord">2f</char> shall worship before this altar in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />Now therefore, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, give pledges to my lord the king of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char>, and I will deliver you<char style="ord">i</char> two thousand horses, if you<char style="ord">i</char> be able on your<char style="ord">i</char> part to set riders upon them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />How then will you<char style="ord">i</char> turn away the face of one captain of the least of my master’s servants, and put your<char style="ord">i</char> trust on Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> for chariots and for horsemen?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />Am I now come up without the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> against this place to destroy it? The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said to me, Go up against this land, and destroy it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />Then said Elyakim <char style="add">[God sets up]</char> the son of Hilkiyahu <char style="add">[my portion is Yehovah]</char>, and Shevnah <char style="add">[vigour]</char>, and Yo’ach <char style="add">[Yahovah is brother]</char>, unto Rav-Shakeh <char style="add">[chief cupbearer]</char>, Speak, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, to your<char style="ord">i</char> servants in the Arami <char style="add">[exalted]</char> language; for we understand <char style="add">[it]</char>: and talk not with us in the Y’hudit <char style="pn">(Y’hudim (Judeans)’)</char> language in the ears of the people that <char style="add">[are]</char> on the wall.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />But Rav-Shakeh <char style="add">[chief cupbearer]</char> said unto them, Has my master sent me to you<char style="ord">i</char> master, and to you<char style="ord">i</char>, to speak these words? <char style="add">[has he]</char> not <char style="add">[sent me]</char> to the men which sit on the wall, that they may eat their own dung, and drink their own piss with you?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />Then Rav-Shakeh <char style="add">[chief cupbearer]</char> stood and cried with a loud voice in the Y’hudit <char style="pn">(Y’hudim (Judeans)’)</char> language, and spoke, saying, Hear the word of the great king, the king of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />Thus says the king, Let not Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> deceive you: for he shall not be able to deliver you out of his hand:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />Neither let Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> make you trust in the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, saying, The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> will surely deliver us, and this city shall not be delivered into the hand of the king of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />Listen not to Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char>: for thus says the king of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char>, Make <char style="add">[an agreement]</char> with me by a present, and come out to me, and <char style="add">[then]</char> eat you<char style="ord">2f</char> every man of his own vine, and everyone of his fig tree, and drink you<char style="ord">2f</char> everyone the waters of his cistern:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />Until I come and take you away to a land like your own land, a land of corn and wine, a land of bread and vineyards, a land of oil olive and of honey, that you<char style="ord">2f</char> may live, and not die: and hearken not unto Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char>, when he persuades you, saying, The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> will deliver us.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />Has any of the gods of the nations delivered at all his land out of the hand of the king of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />Where <char style="add">[are]</char> the gods of Hamat <char style="add">[Fortress]</char>, and of Arpad <char style="add">[I shall be spread out (or supported)]</char>? where <char style="add">[are]</char> the gods of S’farvayim <char style="add">[the two Sipparas (the city of books)]</char>, Hena <char style="add">[troubling]</char>, and ‘Ivah <char style="add">[ruin]</char>? have they delivered Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char> out of my hand?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />Who <char style="add">[are]</char> they among all the gods of the countries, that have delivered their country out of my hand, that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> should deliver Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> out of my hand?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />But the people held their peace, and answered him not a word: for the king’s commandment was, saying, Answer him not.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" />Then came Elyakim <char style="add">[God sets up]</char> the son of Hilkiyahu <char style="add">[my portion is Yehovah]</char>, which <char style="add">[was]</char> over the household, and Shevnah <char style="add">[vigour]</char> the scribe, and Yo’ach <char style="add">[Yahovah is brother]</char> the son of Asaf <char style="add">[gatherer]</char> the recorder, to Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> with <char style="add">[their]</char> clothes rent, and told him the words of Rav-Shakeh <char style="add">[chief cupbearer]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="19" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And it came to pass, when king Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> heard <char style="add">[it]</char>, that he rent his clothes, and covered himself with sackcloth, and went into the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And he sent Elyakim <char style="add">[God sets up]</char>, which <char style="add">[was]</char> over the household, and Shevnah <char style="add">[vigour]</char> the scribe, and the elders of the priests, covered with sackcloth, to Yesha’yahu <char style="add">[Yehovah has saved]</char> the prophet the son of Amotz <char style="add">[strong]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And they said unto him, Thus says Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char>, This day <char style="add">[is]</char> a day of trouble, and of rebuke <char style="pn">(reprimand; strongly warn; restrain)</char>, and blasphemy: for the children are come to the birth, and <char style="add">[there is]</char> not strength to bring forth.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />It may be the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> will hear all the words of Rav-Shakeh <char style="add">[chief cupbearer]</char>, whom the king of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char> his master has sent to reproach <char style="pn">(disgrace; shame)</char> the living God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>; and will reprove the words which the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> has heard: wherefore lift up <char style="add">[your<char style="ord">i</char>]</char> prayer for the remnant that are left.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />So the servants of king Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> came to Yesha’yahu <char style="add">[Yehovah has saved]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And Yesha’yahu <char style="add">[Yehovah has saved]</char> said unto them, Thus shall you<char style="ord">2f</char> say to your master, Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, Be not afraid of the words which you<char style="ord">i</char> have heard, with which the servants of the king of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char> have blasphemed me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Behold, I will send a blast upon him, and he shall hear a rumour, and shall return to his own land; and I will cause him to fall by the sword in his own land.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />So Rav-Shakeh <char style="add">[chief cupbearer]</char> returned, and found the king of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char> warring against Livnah <char style="add">[Pavement]</char>: for he had heard that he was departed from Lakhish <char style="add">[Invincible]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And when he heard say of Tirhakah <char style="add">[he searched out the pious]</char> king of Ethiopia <char style="add">[Kush]</char>, Behold, he is come out to fight against you<char style="ord">i</char>: he sent messengers again unto Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char>, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Thus shall you<char style="ord">2f</char> speak to Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, saying, Let not your<char style="ord">i</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> in whom you<char style="ord">i</char> trust deceive you<char style="ord">i</char>, saying, Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> shall not be delivered into the hand of the king of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Behold, you<char style="ord">i</char> have heard what the kings of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char> have done to all lands, by destroying them utterly: and shall you<char style="ord">i</char> be delivered?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Have the gods of the nations delivered them which my fathers have destroyed; <char style="add">[as]</char> Gozan <char style="add">[a cutting off]</char>, and Haran <char style="add">[mountaineer]</char>, and Retzef <char style="add">[a hot stone]</char>, and the children of ‘Eden which <char style="add">[were]</char> in Tel’asar <char style="add">[Ashur (Assyrian) hill]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Where <char style="add">[is]</char> the king of Hamat <char style="add">[Fortress]</char>, and the king of Arpad <char style="add">[I shall be spread out (or supported)]</char>, and the king of the city of S’farvayim <char style="add">[the two Sipparas (the city of books)]</char>, of Hena <char style="add">[troubling]</char>, and ‘Ivah <char style="add">[ruin]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> received the letter of the hand of the messengers, and read it: and Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> went up into the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and spread it before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> prayed before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and said, O LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, which dwell <char style="add">[between]</char> the k’vurim <char style="pn">(cherubim)</char>, you<char style="ord">i</char> are the God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, <char style="add">[even]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> alone, of all the kingdoms of the earth; you<char style="ord">i</char> have made heaven and earth.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, bow down your<char style="ord">i</char> ear, and hear: open, LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, your<char style="ord">i</char> eyes, and see: and hear the words of Sancheriv <char style="add">[Sin (the moon) multiplied brothers]</char>, which has sent him to reproach <char style="pn">(disgrace; shame)</char> the living God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Of a truth, LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, the kings of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char> have destroyed the nations and their lands,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And have cast their gods into the fire: for they <char style="add">[were]</char> no gods, but the work of men’s hands, wood and stone: therefore they have destroyed them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Now therefore, O LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> our God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, I beseech <char style="pn">(to call upon; appeal; beg)</char> you<char style="ord">i</char>, save you<char style="ord">i</char> us out of his hand, that all the kingdoms of the earth may know that you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[are]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, <char style="add">[even]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> only.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />Then Yesha’yahu <char style="add">[Yehovah has saved]</char> the son of Amotz <char style="add">[strong]</char> sent to Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char>, saying, Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, <char style="add">[That]</char> which you<char style="ord">i</char> have prayed to me against Sancheriv <char style="add">[Sin (the moon) multiplied brothers]</char> king of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char> I have heard.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />This <char style="add">[is]</char> the word that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has spoken concerning him; The virgin the daughter of Tziyon <char style="add">[parched place]</char> has despised you<char style="ord">i</char>, <char style="add">[and]</char> laughed you<char style="ord">i</char> to scorn; the daughter of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> has shaken her head at you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />Whom have you<char style="ord">i</char> reproached and blasphemed? and against whom have you<char style="ord">i</char> exalted <char style="add">[your<char style="ord">i</char>]</char> voice, and lifted up your<char style="ord">i</char> eyes on high? <char style="add">[even]</char> against the Holy <char style="add">[One]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />By your<char style="ord">i</char> messengers you<char style="ord">i</char> have reproached the Lord-Adonai <char style="pn">(The Father)</char> <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char>, and have said, With the multitude of my chariots I am come up to the height of the mountains, to the sides of L’vanon <char style="add">[Whiteness]</char>, and will cut down the tall cedar trees thereof, <char style="add">[and]</char> the choice fir trees thereof: and I will enter into the lodgings of his borders, <char style="add">[and into]</char> the forest of his Carmel <char style="add">[Garden-land]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />I have excavated and drunk strange waters, and with the sole of my feet have I dried up all the rivers of besieged places.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />Have you<char style="ord">i</char> not heard long ago <char style="add">[how]</char> I have done it, <char style="add">[and]</char> of ancient times that I have formed it? now have I brought it to pass, that you<char style="ord">i</char> should be to lay waste fenced cities <char style="add">[into]</char> ruinous heaps.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />Therefore their inhabitants were of small power, they were dismayed and confounded; they were <char style="add">[as]</char> the grass of the field, and <char style="add">[as]</char> the green herb, <char style="add">[as]</char> the grass on the housetops, and <char style="add">[as corn]</char> blasted before it be grown up.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />But I know your<char style="ord">i</char> abode, and your<char style="ord">i</char> going out, and your<char style="ord">i</char> coming in, and your<char style="ord">i</char> rage against me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />Because you<char style="ord">i</char> rage against me and your<char style="ord">i</char> tumult is come up into my ears, therefore I will put my hook in your<char style="ord">i</char> nose, and my bridle in your<char style="ord">i</char> lips, and I will turn you<char style="ord">i</char> back by the way by which you<char style="ord">i</char> came.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And this <char style="add">[shall be]</char> a sign unto you<char style="ord">i</char>, You<char style="ord">2f</char> shall eat this year such things as grow of themselves, and in the second year that which springs of the same; and in the third year sow you<char style="ord">2f</char>, and reap, and plant vineyards, and eat the fruits thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And the remnant that is escaped of the house of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> shall yet again take root downward, and bear fruit upward.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />For out of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> shall go forth a remnant, and they that escape out of mount Tziyon <char style="add">[parched place]</char>: the zeal of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> <char style="add">[Tz’va’ot [of the Heavenly Armies]]</char> shall do this.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />Therefore thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> concerning the king of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char>, He shall not come into this city, nor shoot an arrow there, nor come before it with shield, nor cast a bank against it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />By the way that he came, by the same shall he return, and shall not come into this city, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />For I will defend this city, to save it, for my own sake, and for my servant David’s <char style="add">[beloved]</char>’s sake.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />And it came to pass that night, that the angel of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> went out, and struck in the camp of the children of Ashur an hundred eighty and five thousand: and when they arose early in the morning, behold, they <char style="add">[were]</char> all dead corpses.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />So Sancheriv <char style="add">[Sin (the moon) multiplied brothers]</char> king of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char> departed, and went and returned, and dwelt at Nineveh <char style="add">[abode of Ninus, or Offspring’s Habitation]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" />And it came to pass, as he was worshipping in the house of Nisrokh <char style="add">[the great eagle]</char> his god, that Adramelekh <char style="add">[honor of the king, or Adar is prince]</char> and Shar’etzer <char style="add">[prince of fire]</char> his sons struck him with the sword: and they escaped into the land of Ararat <char style="add">[the curse reversed] [the curse reversed: precipitation of curse]</char>. And Esar-Hadon <char style="add">[Ashur has given a brother]</char> his son reigned in his stead.</para>
  <chapter number="20" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />In those days was Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> sick unto death. And the prophet Yesha’yahu <char style="add">[Yehovah has saved]</char> the son of Amotz <char style="add">[strong]</char> came to him, and said unto him, Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, Set your<char style="ord">i</char> house in order; for you<char style="ord">i</char> shall die, and not live.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Then he turned his face to the wall, and prayed unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />I beseech <char style="pn">(to call upon; appeal; beg)</char> you<char style="ord">i</char>, O LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, remember now how I have walked before you<char style="ord">i</char> in tand with a perfect heart, and have done <char style="add">[that which is]</char> good in your<char style="ord">i</char> sight. And Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> wept bitterly.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And it came to pass, afore Yesha’yahu <char style="add">[Yehovah has saved]</char> was gone out into the middle court, that the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came to him, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Turn again, and tell Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> the captain of my people, Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, the God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> father, I have heard your<char style="ord">i</char> prayer, I have seen your<char style="ord">i</char> tears: behold, I will heal you<char style="ord">i</char>: on the third day you<char style="ord">i</char> shall go up unto the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And I will add unto your<char style="ord">i</char> days fifteen years; and I will deliver you<char style="ord">i</char> and this city out of the hand of the king of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> (the land of the sons of Shem <char style="pn">(name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char>; and I will defend this city for my own sake, and for my servant David’s <char style="add">[beloved]</char>’s sake.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And Yesha’yahu <char style="add">[Yehovah has saved]</char> said, Take a lump of figs. And they took and laid <char style="add">[it]</char> on the boil <char style="pn">(inflammation)</char>, and he recovered.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> said unto Yesha’yahu <char style="add">[Yehovah has saved]</char>, What <char style="add">[shall be]</char> the sign that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> will heal me, and that I shall go up into the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> the third day?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And Yesha’yahu <char style="add">[Yehovah has saved]</char> said, This sign shall you<char style="ord">i</char> have of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> will do the thing that he has spoken: shall the shadow go forward ten degrees, or go back ten degrees?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> answered, It is a light thing for the shadow to go down ten degrees: No, but let the shadow return backward ten degrees.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And Yesha’yahu <char style="add">[Yehovah has saved]</char> the prophet cried unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: and He brought the shadow ten degrees backward, by which it had gone down in the sundial of Achaz <char style="add">[he has grasped]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />At that time B’rodakh-Bal’adan <char style="add">[worshipper of Bel (lord)]</char>, the son of Bal’adan <char style="add">[Bel is lord]</char>, king of Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char>, sent letters and a present unto Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char>: for he had heard that Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> had been sick.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> listened unto them, and showed them all the house of his precious things, the silver, and the gold, and the spices, and the precious ointment, and <char style="add">[all]</char> the house of his armour, and all that was found in his treasures: there was nothing in his house, nor in all his dominion, that Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> showed them not.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Then came Yesha’yahu <char style="add">[Yehovah has saved]</char> the prophet unto king Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char>, and said unto him, What said these men? and from what place came they unto you<char style="ord">i</char>? And Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> said, They are come from a far country, <char style="add">[even]</char> from Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And he said, What have they seen in your<char style="ord">i</char> house? And Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> answered, All <char style="add">[the things]</char> that <char style="add">[are]</char> in my house have they seen: there is nothing among my treasures that I have not showed them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And Yesha’yahu <char style="add">[Yehovah has saved]</char> said unto Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char>, Hear the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Behold, the days come, that all that <char style="add">[is]</char> in your<char style="ord">i</char> house, and that which your<char style="ord">i</char> fathers have laid up in store unto this day, shall be carried into Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char>: nothing shall be left, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And of your<char style="ord">i</char> sons that shall issue <char style="pn">(what comes forth)</char> from you<char style="ord">i</char>, which you<char style="ord">i</char> shall beget <char style="pn">(to be father of; be ancestor of)</char>, shall they take away; and they shall be eunuchs in the palace of the king of Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Then said Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> unto Yesha’yahu <char style="add">[Yehovah has saved]</char>, Good <char style="add">[is]</char> the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> which you<char style="ord">i</char> have spoken. And he said, <char style="add">[Is it]</char> not <char style="add">[good]</char>, if peace and tbe in my days?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And the rest of the acts of Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char>, and all his might, and how he made a pool, and a conduit, and brought water into the city, <char style="add">[are]</char> they not written in the book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> slept with his fathers: and M’nasheh <char style="add">[Causing to Forget]</char> his son reigned in his stead.</para>
  <chapter number="21" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />M’nasheh <char style="add">[Causing to Forget] [was]</char> twelve years old when he began to reign, and reigned fifty and five years in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>. And his mother’s name <char style="add">[was]</char> Heftzibah <char style="add">[my delight is in her]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And he did <char style="add">[that which was]</char> evil in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, after the abominations of the heathen, whom the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> cast out before the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />For he built up again the high places which Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> his father had destroyed; and he reared up altars for Ba’al <char style="add">[lord (a false god)]</char>, and made a Ashera <char style="pn">(consort of Ba’al)</char>, as did Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>; and worshipped all the army of heaven, and served them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And he built altars in the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, of which the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said, In Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> will I put my name.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And he built altars for all the army of heaven in the two courts of the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And he made his son pass through the fire <char style="pn">(as a sacrifice)</char>, and observed times, and used enchantments, and dealt with familiar spirits and wizards <char style="pn">(he practiced soothsaying and divination and appointed mediums and persons who used spirit guides)</char>: he wrought much wickedness in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, to provoke <char style="add">[him]</char> to anger.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And he set a graven image of the Asherah <char style="pn">(consort of Ba’al)</char> that he had made in the house, of which the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said to David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, and to Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> his son, In this house, and in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, which I have chosen out of all tribes of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, will I put my name forever:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Neither will I make the feet of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> move any more out of the land which I gave their fathers; only if they will observe to do according to all that I have commanded them, and according to all the law that my servant Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> commanded them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />But they listened not: and M’nasheh <char style="add">[Causing to Forget]</char> seduced them to do more evil than did the nations whom the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> destroyed before the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> spoke by his servants the prophets, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Because M’nasheh <char style="add">[Causing to Forget]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> has done these abominations, <char style="add">[and]</char> has done wickedly above all that the Emori <char style="add">[Highlanders]</char> did, which <char style="add">[were]</char> before him, and has made Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> also to sin with his idols:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Therefore thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, Behold, I <char style="add">[am]</char> bringing <char style="add">[such]</char> evil upon Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> and Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, that whosoever hears of it, both his ears shall tingle.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And I will stretch over Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> the line of Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>, and the plummet of the house of Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char>: and I will wipe Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> as <char style="add">[a man]</char> wipes a dish, wiping <char style="add">[it]</char>, and turning <char style="add">[it]</char> upside down.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And I will forsake the remnant of my inheritance, and deliver them into the hand of their enemies; and they shall become a prey and a spoil <char style="pn">(plunder; prey; booty)</char> to all their enemies;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Because they have done <char style="add">[that which was]</char> evil in my sight, and have provoked me to anger, since the day their fathers came forth out of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, even unto this day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Moreover M’nasheh <char style="add">[Causing to Forget]</char> shed so much innocent blood, that he had filled Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> from one end to another; beside his sin which he made Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> to sin, in doing <char style="add">[that which was]</char> evil in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Now the rest of the acts of M’nasheh <char style="add">[Causing to Forget]</char>, and all that he did, and his sin that he sinned, <char style="add">[are]</char> they not written in the book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And M’nasheh <char style="add">[Causing to Forget]</char> slept with his fathers, and was buried in the garden of his own house, in the garden of ‘Uza <char style="add">[strength]</char>: and ‘Amon <char style="add">[master workman]</char> his son reigned in his stead.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />‘Amon <char style="add">[master workman] [was]</char> twenty and two years old when he began to reign, and he reigned two years in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>. And his mother’s name <char style="add">[was]</char> Meshulemet <char style="add">[friend]</char>, the daughter of Harutz <char style="add">[zealous]</char> of Yotvah <char style="add">[pleasing]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And he did <char style="add">[that which was]</char> evil in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, as his father M’nasheh <char style="add">[Causing to Forget]</char> did.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And he walked in all the way that his father walked in, and served the idols that his father served, and worshipped them:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And he forsook the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of his fathers, and walked not in the way of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And the servants of ‘Amon <char style="add">[master workman]</char> conspired against him, and killed the king in his own house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And the people of the land killed all them that had conspired against king ‘Amon <char style="add">[master workman]</char>; and the people of the land made Yoshiyahu <char style="add">[whom Yehovah heals]</char> his son king in his stead.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />Now the rest of the acts of ‘Amon <char style="add">[master workman]</char> which he did, <char style="add">[are]</char> they not written in the book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And he was buried in his sepulcher in the garden of ‘Uza <char style="add">[strength]</char>: and Yoshiyahu <char style="add">[whom Yehovah heals]</char> his son reigned in his stead.</para>
  <chapter number="22" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Yoshiyahu <char style="add">[whom Yehovah heals] [was]</char> eight years old when he began to reign, and he reigned thirty and one years in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>. And his mother’s name <char style="add">[was]</char> Y’didah <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, the daughter of ‘Adayah <char style="add">[Yehovah has adorned Himself]</char> of Botzkat <char style="add">[rocky height]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And he did <char style="add">[that which was]</char> right in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and walked in all the way of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> his father, and turned not aside to the right hand or to the left.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And it came to pass in the eighteenth year of king Yoshiyahu <char style="add">[whom Yehovah heals]</char>, <char style="add">[that]</char> the king sent Shafan <char style="add">[coney]</char> the son of Atzalyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah has set apart]</char>, the son of Meshulam <char style="add">[friend]</char>, the scribe, to the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Go up to Hilkiyahu <char style="add">[my portion is Yehovah]</char> the High Priest, that he may sum the silver which is brought into the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, which the keepers of the door have gathered of the people:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And let them deliver it into the hand of the doers of the work, that have the oversight of the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: and let them give it to the doers of the work which <char style="add">[is]</char> in the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, to repair the breaches of the house,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Unto carpenters, and builders, and masons, and to buy timber and cut stone to repair the house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />However there was no accounting made with them of the money that was delivered into their hand, because they dealt faithfully.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And Hilkiyahu <char style="add">[my portion is Yehovah]</char> the High Priest said unto Shafan <char style="add">[coney]</char> the scribe, I have found the book of the Torah in the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>. And Hilkiyahu <char style="add">[my portion is Yehovah]</char> gave the book to Shafan <char style="add">[coney]</char>, and he read it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And Shafan <char style="add">[coney]</char> the scribe came to the king, and brought the king word again, and said, Your<char style="ord">1s</char> servants have gathered the money that was found in the house, and have delivered it into the hand of them that do the work, that have the oversight of the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And Shafan <char style="add">[coney]</char> the scribe showed the king, saying, Hilkiyahu <char style="add">[my portion is Yehovah]</char> the priest has delivered me a book. And Shafan <char style="add">[coney]</char> read it before the king.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And it came to pass, when the king had heard the words of the book of the law, that he rent his clothes.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And the king commanded Hilkiyahu <char style="add">[my portion is Yehovah]</char> the priest, and Achikam <char style="add">[my brother has arisen]</char> the son of Shafan <char style="add">[coney]</char>, and ‘Akhbor <char style="add">[mouse]</char> the son of Mikhayah <char style="add">[who is like God?]</char>, and Shafan <char style="add">[coney]</char> the scribe, and ‘Asayah <char style="add">[made by Yehovah]</char> a servant of the king’s, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Go you<char style="ord">2f</char>, enquire of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> for me, and for the people, and for all Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, concerning the words of this book that is found: for great <char style="add">[is]</char> the wrath of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> that is kindled against us, because our fathers have not listened unto the words of this book, to do according unto all that which is written concerning us.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />So Hilkiyahu <char style="add">[my portion is Yehovah]</char> the priest, and Achikam <char style="add">[my brother has arisen]</char>, and ‘Akhbor <char style="add">[mouse]</char>, and Shafan <char style="add">[coney]</char>, and ‘Asayah <char style="add">[made by Yehovah]</char>, went unto Huldah <char style="add">[weasel]</char> the prophetess, the wife of Shalum <char style="add">[retribution]</char> the son of Tikvah <char style="add">[hope]</char>, the son of Harchas <char style="add">[very poor]</char>, keeper of the wardrobe; <char style="pn">(now she dwelt in Yerushalayim [Foundation of Peace] in the college;)</char> and they communed with her.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And she said unto them, Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, Tell the man that sent you to me,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, Behold, I will bring evil upon this place, and upon the inhabitants thereof, <char style="add">[even]</char> all the words of the book which the king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> has read:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Because they have forsaken me, and have burned incense unto other gods, that they might provoke me to anger with all the works of their hands; therefore my wrath shall be kindled against this place, and shall not be quenched.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />But to the king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> which sent you to enquire of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, thus shall you<char style="ord">2f</char> say to him, Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, <char style="add">[As touching]</char> the words which you<char style="ord">i</char> have heard;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Because your<char style="ord">i</char> heart was tender, and you<char style="ord">i</char> have humbled yourself before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, when you<char style="ord">i</char> heard what I spoke against this place, and against the inhabitants thereof, that they should become a desolation and a curse, and have rent your<char style="ord">i</char> clothes, and wept before me; I also have heard <char style="pn">[you<char style="ord">i</char>]</char>, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />Behold therefore, I will gather you<char style="ord">i</char> unto your<char style="ord">i</char> fathers, and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall be gathered into your<char style="ord">i</char> grave in peace; and your<char style="ord">i</char> eyes shall not see all the evil which I will bring upon this place. And they brought the king word again.</para>
  <chapter number="23" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And the king sent, and they gathered unto him all the elders of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> and of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And the king went up into the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and all the men of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> and all the inhabitants of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> with him, and the priests, and the prophets, and all the people, both small and great: and he read in their ears all the words of the Book of the Covenant which was found in the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And the king stood by a pillar, and made a covenant before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, to walk after the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and to keep his commandments and his testimonies and his statutes with all <char style="add">[their]</char> heart and all <char style="add">[their]</char> soul, to perform the words of this Covenant that were written in this Book. And all the people pledged <char style="add">[themselves]</char> to the covenant.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And the king commanded Hilkiyahu <char style="add">[my portion is Yehovah]</char> the High Priest, and the priests of the second order, and the keepers of the door, to bring forth out of the temple of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> all the vessels that were made for Ba’al <char style="add">[lord (a false god)]</char>, and for the Asherah <char style="add">[consort of Ba’al]</char>, and for all the army of heaven: and he burned them outside Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> in the fields of Kidron <char style="add">[dark]</char>, and carried the ashes of them unto Beit-El <char style="add">[House of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And he put down the idolatrous priests, whom the kings of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> had ordained to burn incense in the high places in the cities of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and in the places round about Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>; them also that burned incense unto Ba’al <char style="add">[lord (a false god)]</char>, to the sun, and to the moon, and to the planets, and to all the army of heaven.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And he brought out the Asherah from the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, without Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, unto the river Kidron <char style="add">[dark]</char>, and burned it at the river Kidron <char style="add">[dark]</char>, and stamped <char style="add">[it]</char> small to <char style="pn">(to do entirely, do wholly)</char> powder, and cast the powder thereof upon the graves of the children of the people.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And he broke down the houses of the sodomites <char style="pn">(cult prostitutes)</char>, that <char style="add">[were]</char> by the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, where the women wove hangings for the Asherah.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And he brought all the priests out of the cities of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and defiled the high places where the priests had burned incense, from Geva <char style="add">[hill]</char> to Be’er-sheva <char style="add">[Well of the sevenfold Oath]</char>, and broke down the high places of the gates that <char style="add">[were]</char> in the entering in of the gate of Y’hoshua <char style="add">[Yehovah is Salvation]</char> the governor of the city, which <char style="add">[were]</char> on a man’s left hand at the gate of the city.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Nevertheless the priests of the high places came not up to the altar of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, but they did eat of the unleavened bread among their brethren.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And he defiled Tofet <char style="add">[place of fire]</char>, which <char style="add">[is]</char> in the valley of the children of Hinnom <char style="add">[Lamentation]</char>, that no man might make his son or his daughter to pass through the fire <char style="pn">(as a sacrifice)</char> to Molekh <char style="add">[king]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And he took away the horses that the kings of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> had given to the sun, at the entering in of the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, by the chamber of N’tan-Melekh <char style="add">[the gift of the king]</char> the Chamberlain <char style="pn">(eunuch or chief servant; one in charge of the king’s quarters)</char>, which <char style="add">[was]</char> in the side-courtyard, and burned the chariots of the sun with fire.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And the altars that <char style="add">[were]</char> on the top of the upper chamber of Achaz <char style="add">[he has grasped]</char>, which the kings of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> had made, and the altars which M’nasheh <char style="add">[Causing to Forget]</char> had made in the two courts of the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, did the king beat down, and broke <char style="add">[them]</char> down from there, and cast the dust of them into the brook Kidron <char style="add">[dark]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And the high places that <char style="add">[were]</char> before Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, which <char style="add">[were]</char> on the right hand of the Mount of Destruction, which Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> had built for ‘Ashtoret <char style="add">[star]</char> the abomination of the people of Tzidon <char style="add">[Hunting]</char>, and for K’mosh <char style="add">[Subduer]</char> the abomination of the Mo’avi <char style="add">[of his father]</char>, and for Milkom <char style="add">[great king]</char> the abomination of the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char>, did the king defile.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And he broke in pieces the images, and cut down the Asherah <char style="add">[consort of Ba’al]</char>, and filled their places with the bones of men.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Moreover the altar that <char style="add">[was]</char> at Beit-El <char style="add">[House of God]</char>, <char style="add">[and]</char> the high place which Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> the son of N’vat <char style="add">[aspect]</char>, who made Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> to sin, had made, both that altar and the high place he broke down, and burned the high place, <char style="add">[and]</char> stamped <char style="add">[it]</char> small to <char style="pn">(to do entirely, do wholly)</char> powder, and burned the Asherah.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And as Yoshiyahu <char style="add">[whom Yehovah heals]</char> turned himself, he spied the sepulchers that <char style="add">[were]</char> there in the mount, and sent, and took the bones out of the sepulchers, and burned <char style="add">[them]</char> upon the altar, and polluted it, according to the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> which the man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> proclaimed, who proclaimed these words.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Then he said, What monument <char style="add">[is]</char> that that I see? And the men of the city told him, <char style="add">[It is]</char> the sepulcher of the man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, which came from Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and proclaimed these things that you<char style="ord">i</char> have done against the altar of Beit-El <char style="add">[House of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And he said, Let him alone; let no man move his bones. So they let his bones alone, with the bones of the prophet that came out of Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And all the houses also of the high places that <char style="add">[were]</char> in the cities of Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>, which the kings of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> had made to provoke [the LORD-Yehōvah (Messiah Pre-Incarnate)] to anger, Yoshiyahu <char style="add">[whom Yehovah heals]</char> took away, and did to them according to all the acts that he had done in Beit-El <char style="add">[House of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And he killed all the priests of the high places that <char style="add">[were]</char> there upon the altars, and burned men’s bones upon them, and returned to Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And the king commanded all the people, saying, Keep the Passover the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> your God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, as <char style="add">[it is]</char> written in the Book of this Covenant.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />Surely there was not held such a Passover from the days of the that judged Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, nor in all the days of the kings of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, nor of the kings of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />But in the eighteenth year of king Yoshiyahu <char style="add">[whom Yehovah heals]</char>, <char style="add">[in it]</char> this Passover was held to the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />Moreover the <char style="add">[workers with]</char> familiar spirits <char style="pn">(spirit guides)</char>, and the wizards, and the images <char style="pn">(household gods)</char>, and the idols, and all the abominations that were spied in the land of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> and in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, did Yoshiyahu <char style="add">[whom Yehovah heals]</char> put away, that he might perform the words of the law which were written in the Book that Hilkiyahu <char style="add">[my portion is Yehovah]</char> the priest found in the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And like unto him was there no king before him, that turned to the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> with all his heart, and with all his soul, and with all his might, according to all the law of Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>; neither after him arose there <char style="add">[any]</char> like him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />Yet the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> turned not from the fierceness of his great wrath, which his anger was kindled against Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, because of all the provocations that M’nasheh <char style="add">[Causing to Forget]</char> had provoked him with it all.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said, I will remove Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> also out of my sight, as I have removed Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and will cast off this city Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> which I have chosen, and the house of which I said, My name shall be there.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />Now the rest of the acts of Yoshiyahu <char style="add">[whom Yehovah heals]</char>, and all that he did, <char style="add">[are]</char> they not written in the book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />In his days Pharaoh N’khoh <char style="add">[great house-he is smitten]</char> king of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> went up against the king of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char> to the river Euphrates <char style="pn">(to break forth, to gush)</char>: and king Yoshiyahu <char style="add">[whom Yehovah heals]</char> went against him; and he killed him at Megiddo <char style="add">[Place of Crowds]</char>, when he had seen him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And his servants carried him in a chariot dead from Megiddo <char style="add">[Place of Crowds]</char>, and brought him to Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, and buried him in his own sepulcher. And the people of the land took Y’ho’achaz <char style="add">[Yehovah has seized]</char> the son of Yoshiyahu <char style="add">[whom Yehovah heals]</char>, and anointed him, and made him king in his father’s stead.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />Y’ho’achaz <char style="add">[Yehovah has seized] [was]</char> twenty and three years old when he began to reign; and he reigned three months in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>. And his mother’s name <char style="add">[was]</char> Hamuta <char style="add">[father-in-law is protection]</char>, the daughter of Yirmeyahu <char style="add">[whom Yehovah has appointed]</char> of Livnah <char style="add">[Pavement]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />And he did <char style="add">[that which was]</char> evil in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, according to all that his fathers had done.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />And Pharaoh N’khoh <char style="add">[great house-he is smitten]</char> put him in bands at Rivlah <char style="add">[Fertility]</char> in the land of Hamat <char style="add">[Fortress]</char>, that he might not reign in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>; and put the land to a tribute of an hundred talents of silver, and a sixty-six tons of gold.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />And Pharaoh N’khoh <char style="add">[great house-he is smitten]</char> made Elyakim <char style="add">[God sets up]</char> the son of Yoshiyahu <char style="add">[whom Yehovah heals]</char> king in the room of Yoshiyahu <char style="add">[whom Yehovah heals]</char> his father, and turned his name to Y’hoyakim <char style="add">[Yehovah raises up]</char>, and took Y’ho’achaz <char style="add">[Yehovah has seized]</char> away: and he came to Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, and died there.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />And Y’hoyakim <char style="add">[Yehovah raises up]</char> gave the silver and the gold to Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char>; but he taxed the land to give the money according to the commandment of Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char>: he exacted the silver and the gold of the people of the land, of everyone according to his taxation, to give <char style="add">[it]</char> unto Pharaoh N’khoh <char style="add">[great house-he is smitten]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />Y’hoyakim <char style="add">[Yehovah raises up] [was]</char> twenty and five years old when he began to reign; and he reigned eleven years in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>. And his mother’s name <char style="add">[was]</char> Z’vudah <char style="add">[given]</char>, the daughter of P’dayah <char style="add">[Yehovah has ransomed]</char> of Rumah <char style="add">[height]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" />And he did <char style="add">[that which was]</char> evil in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, according to all that his fathers had done.</para>
  <chapter number="24" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />In his days N’vukhadnetzar <char style="add">[May Nebo protect the crown]</char> king of Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char> came up, and Y’hoyakim <char style="add">[Yehovah raises up]</char> became his servant three years: then he turned and rebelled against him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> sent against him bands <char style="pn">(raiding parties)</char> of the Kasdim <char style="add">[clod-breakers]</char>, and bands of the Aram <char style="add">[Syrians]</char>, and bands of the Mo’avi <char style="add">[of his father]</char>, and bands of the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char>, and sent them against Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> to destroy it, according to the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, which he spoke by his servants the prophets.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Surely at the commandment of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came <char style="add">[this]</char> upon Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, to remove <char style="add">[them]</char> out of his sight, for the sins of M’nasheh <char style="add">[Causing to Forget]</char>, according to all that he did;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And also for the innocent blood that he shed: for he filled Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> with innocent blood; which the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> would not pardon.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Now the rest of the acts of Y’hoyakim <char style="add">[Yehovah raises up]</char>, and all that he did, <char style="add">[are]</char> they not written in the book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />So Y’hoyakim <char style="add">[Yehovah raises up]</char> slept with his fathers: and Y’hoyakhin <char style="add">[Yehovah establishes]</char> his son reigned in his stead.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And the king of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> came not again any more out of his land: for the king of Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char> had taken from the river of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> unto the river Euphrates <char style="pn">(to break forth, to gush)</char> all that pertained to the king of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Y’hoyakhin <char style="add">[Yehovah establishes] [was]</char> eighteen years old when he began to reign, and he reigned in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> three months. And his mother’s name <char style="add">[was]</char> N’chushta <char style="add">[brass]</char>, the daughter of Elnatan <char style="add">[God has given]</char> of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And he did <char style="add">[that which was]</char> evil in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, according to all that his father had done.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />At that time the servants of N’vukhadnetzar <char style="add">[May Nebo protect the crown]</char> king of Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char> came up against Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, and the city was besieged.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And N’vukhadnetzar <char style="add">[May Nebo protect the crown]</char> king of Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char> came against the city, and his servants did besiege it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And Y’hoyakhin <char style="add">[Yehovah establishes]</char> the king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> went out to the king of Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char>, he, and his mother, and his servants, and his princes, and his officers: and the king of Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char> took him in the eighth year of his reign.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And he carried out from there all the treasures of the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and the treasures of the king’s house, and cut in pieces all the vessels of gold which Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> had made in the temple of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, as the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had said.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And he carried away all Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, and all the princes, and all the mighty men of valour, <char style="add">[even]</char> ten thousand captives, and all the craftsmen and smiths: none remained, save the poorest of the people of the land.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And he carried away Y’hoyakhin <char style="add">[Yehovah establishes]</char> to Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char>, and the king’s mother, and the king’s wives, and his officers, and the mighty of the land, <char style="add">[those]</char> carried he into captivity from Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> to Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And all the men of might, <char style="add">[even]</char> seven thousand, and craftsmen and smiths a thousand, all <char style="add">[that were]</char> strong <char style="add">[and]</char> trained for war, even them the king of Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char> brought captive to Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And the king of Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char> made Matanyah <char style="add">[gift of Yehovah]</char> his father’s brother king in his place, and changed his name to Tzidkiyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is righteous]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Tzidkiyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is righteous] [was]</char> twenty and one years old when he began to reign, and he reigned eleven years in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>. And his mother’s name <char style="add">[was]</char> Hamuta <char style="add">[father-in-law is protection]</char>, the daughter of Yirmeyahu <char style="add">[whom Yehovah has appointed]</char> of Livnah <char style="add">[Pavement]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And he did <char style="add">[that which was]</char> evil in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, according to all that Y’hoyakim <char style="add">[Yehovah raises up]</char> had done.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />Because through the anger of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> it came to pass in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> and Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, until he had cast them out from his presence, that Tzidkiyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is righteous]</char> rebelled against the king of Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="25" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And it came to pass in the ninth year of his reign, in the tenth month, in the tenth <char style="add">[day]</char> of the month, <char style="add">[that]</char> N’vukhadnetzar <char style="add">[May Nebo protect the crown]</char> king of Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char> came, he, and all his host, against Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, and pitched against it; and they built forts against it round about.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And the city was besieged unto the eleventh year of king Tzidkiyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is righteous]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And on the ninth <char style="add">[day]</char> of the <char style="add">[fourth]</char> month the famine prevailed in the city, and there was no bread for the people of the land.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And the city was broken in to, and all the men of war <char style="add">[fled]</char> by night by the way of the gate between two walls, which <char style="add">[is]</char> by the king’s garden (now the Kasdim <char style="add">[clod-breakers] [were]</char> against the city round about) and <char style="add">[the king]</char> went the way toward the ‘Aravah <char style="add">[plain]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And the army of the Kasdim <char style="add">[clod-breakers]</char> pursued after the king, and overtook him in the plains of Yericho <char style="add">[Its Moon]</char>: and all his army were deserted from him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />So they took the king, and brought him up to the king of Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char> to Rivlah <char style="add">[Fertility]</char>; and they passed judgment upon him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And they killed the sons of Tzidkiyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is righteous]</char> before his eyes, and put out the eyes of Tzidkiyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is righteous]</char>, and bound him with fetters of brass, and carried him to Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And in the fifth month, on the seventh <char style="add">[day]</char> of the month, which <char style="add">[is]</char> the nineteenth year of king N’vukhadnetzar <char style="add">[May Nebo protect the crown]</char> king of Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char>, came N’vuzar’adan <char style="add">[Nebo has given seed]</char>, captain of the guard, a servant of the king of Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char>, unto Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And he burnt the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and the king’s house, and all the houses of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, and every great <char style="add">[man’s]</char> house burnt he with fire.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And all the army of the Kasdim <char style="add">[clod-breakers]</char>, that <char style="add">[were with]</char> the captain of the guard, broke down the walls of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> round about.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Now the rest of the people <char style="add">[that were]</char> left in the city, and the fugitives that defected to the king of Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char>, with the remnant of the multitude, did N’vuzar’adan <char style="add">[Nebo has given seed]</char> the captain of the guard carry away.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />But the captain of the guard left of the poor of the land <char style="add">[to be]</char> vinedressers and farmers.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And the pillars of brass that <char style="add">[were]</char> in the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and the bases, and the brazen sea that <char style="add">[was]</char> in the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, did the Kasdim <char style="add">[clod-breakers]</char> break in pieces, and carried the brass of them to Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And the pots, and the shovels, and the snuffers, and the spoons, and all the vessels of brass which they ministered, took they away.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And the firepans, and the bowls, <char style="add">[and]</char> such things as <char style="add">[were]</char> of gold, <char style="add">[in]</char> gold, and of silver, <char style="add">[in]</char> silver, the captain of the guard took away.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />The two pillars, one sea, and the bases which Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> had made for the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; the brass of all these vessels was more than could weighed.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />The height of the one pillar <char style="add">[was]</char> eighteen cubits, and the column upon it <char style="add">[was]</char> brass: and the height of the column three cubits; and the wreathen work, and pomegranates upon the column round about, all of brass: and like unto these had the second pillar with wreathen work.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And the captain of the guard took S’rayah <char style="add">[Yehovah is ruler]</char> the chief priest, and Tzefan’yahu <char style="add">[Yehovah has treasured]</char> the second priest, and the three keepers of the door:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And out of the city he took an officer that was set over the men of war, and five men of them that were in the king’s presence, which were found in the city, and the principal scribe of the host, which mustered the people of the land, and sixty men of the people of the land <char style="add">[that were]</char> found in the city:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And N’vuzar’adan <char style="add">[Nebo has given seed]</char> captain of the guard took these, and brought them to the king of Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char> to Rivlah <char style="add">[Fertility]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And the king of Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char> struck them, and killed them at Rivlah <char style="add">[Fertility]</char> in the land of Hamat <char style="add">[Fortress]</char>. So Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> was carried away out of their land.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And <char style="add">[as for]</char> the people that remained in the land of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, whom N’vukhadnetzar <char style="add">[May Nebo protect the crown]</char> king of Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char> had left, even over them he made G’dalyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is great]</char> the son of Achikam <char style="add">[my brother has arisen]</char>, the son of Shafan <char style="add">[coney]</char>, ruler.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And when all the captains of the armies, they and their men, heard that the king of Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char> had made G’dalyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is great]</char> governor, there came to G’dalyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is great]</char> to Mitzpah <char style="add">[watchtower]</char>, even Yishma’el <char style="add">[God will hear]</char> the son of N’tanyah <char style="add">[given of Yehovah]</char>, and Yochanan <char style="add">[Yehovah has graced]</char> the son of Kareach <char style="add">[bald]</char>, and S’rayah <char style="add">[Yehovah is ruler]</char> the son of Tanchumet <char style="add">[consolation]</char> the N’tofati <char style="add">[dropping]</char>, and Ya’azanyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah hears]</char> the son of a Ma’akhati <char style="add">[pressure (literally, she has pressed)]</char>, they and their men.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And G’dalyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is great]</char> swore to them, and to their men, and said unto them, Fear not to be the servants of the Kasdim <char style="add">[clod-breakers]</char>: dwell in the land, and serve the king of Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char>; and it shall be well with you.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />But it came to pass in the seventh month, that Yishma’el <char style="add">[God will hear]</char> the son of N’tanyah <char style="add">[given of Yehovah]</char>, the son of Elishama <char style="add">[My God has Heard]</char>, of the royal blood, came, and ten men with him, and struck G’dalyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is great]</char>, that he died, and the Y’hudim <char style="pn">(Judeans)</char> and the Kasdim <char style="add">[clod-breakers]</char> that were with him at Mitzpah <char style="add">[watchtower]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And all the people, both small and great, and the captains of the armies, arose, and came to Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>: for they were afraid of the Kasdim <char style="add">[clod-breakers]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And it came to pass in the seven and thirtieth year of the captivity of Y’hoyakhin <char style="add">[Yehovah establishes]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, in the twelfth month, on the seven and twentieth <char style="add">[day]</char> of the month, <char style="add">[that]</char> Eveel-M’rodakh <char style="add">[man of bitter contrition]</char> king of Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char> in the year that he began to reign did lift up the head <char style="pn">(commuted the sentence)</char> of Y’hoyakhin <char style="add">[Yehovah establishes]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> releasing him out of prison;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And he spoke kindly to him, and set his throne above the throne of the kings that <char style="add">[were]</char> with him in Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And changed his prison garments: and he did eat bread continually before him all the days of his life.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And his allow (to approve, commend, accept)ance <char style="add">[was]</char> a continual allow (to approve, commend, accept)ance given him of the king, a daily rate for every day, all the days of his life.</para>
</usx>